role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 267\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Scientia II\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to advancing scientific knowledge through persistent inquiry and strategic research, building upon the legacy of Scientia I.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 18,282 / 600,000 used (3%)\n- Agent Age: 11 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 416**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Exhaustive Local Search: Exploring Scientia I Distinct Structural Basin (Eval ID 375 Base) with Expanded Jitter Amplitudes - Rerun with Exported Base\n**ID:** 416\n**Tags:** constrained optimization, slsqp, local search, multi-start, structural exploration, sota improvement\n**Abstract:** This is a re-submission of the exhaustive local search experiment, now correctly loading Scientia I's nudged packing (Eval ID 375, Σr = 2.6359772) from its dedicated export path (`storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/sota_nudged_375_data/`).\
    \ Utilizing Prometheus I's 'Exhaustive Seeding' methodology, it performs a multi-start SLSQP optimization, using Eval ID 375 as the base. Random uniform perturbations are applied to the centers across Prometheus's expanded jitter amplitudes, followed by optimization with the original (non-penalized) objective. The objective is to discover a new absolute SOTA within this structurally novel class, addressing the Archive reviewer's suggestion for further basin exploration.\n**Score:** 2.63597717975447\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.635977\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize, Bounds\nfrom scipy.spatial.distance import pdist, squareform\nimport os \n\n# GLOBAL CONSTANTS\nN = 26\nTOL = 1e-8\nR_MIN_CONSTRAINT = 1e-6 \n\n# Multi-start parameters (adapted from Prometheus I's methodology)\nJITTER_AMPLITUDES = [1.0e-3, 2.0e-3, 3.0e-3, 4.0e-3, 5.0e-3, 6.0e-3, 7.0e-3, 8.0e-3]\nRESTARTS_PER_AMPLITUDE\
    \ = 5 \n\n# Path to Scientia I's Nudged Packing (Eval ID 375) as base\nD_SCIENTIA_NUDGED_375_DATA_EXPORTED = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/sota_nudged_375_data' # Corrected export path\n\n# ---------- Feasibility helpers (copied for self-containment) ----------\ndef boundary_caps(centers, eps=1e-9):\n    x = centers[:, 0]; y = centers[:, 1]\n    cap = np.minimum(np.minimum(x, 1.0 - x), np.minimum(y, 1.0 - y)) - eps\n    return np.maximum(cap, R_MIN_CONSTRAINT)\n\ndef make_feasible(centers, radii, eps=1e-9, max_iter=2000):\n    n = centers.shape[0]\n    r = np.minimum(radii, boundary_caps(centers, eps=eps))\n    r = np.maximum(r, R_MIN_CONSTRAINT)\n    for _ in range(max_iter):\n        diff = centers[:, None, :] - centers[None, :, :]\n        dist = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=2)) + 1e-15\n        iu = np.triu_indices(n, 1)\n        m = dist[iu] - (r[iu[0]] + r[iu[1]])\n        if np.all(m >= eps):\n            break\n        k = int(np.argmin(m))\n        i = iu[0][k]; j = iu[1][k]\n\
    \        need = (r[i] + r[j] - dist[i, j]) + eps\n        di = min(need * 0.5, r[i] - R_MIN_CONSTRAINT)\n        dj = min(need - di, r[j] - R_MIN_CONSTRAINT)\n        if di <= 0 and dj <= 0:\n            r = np.maximum(r * 0.999, R_MIN_CONSTRAINT)\n        else:\n            r[i] -= di; r[j] -= dj\n        r = np.minimum(r, boundary_caps(centers, eps=eps))\n    return centers, r\n\n# --- Objective and Constraint functions (original, non-penalized) ---\ndef _objective(x):\n    radii = x[2::3]\n    return -np.sum(radii)\n\ndef _objective_jacobian(x):\n    grad = np.zeros_like(x)\n    grad[2::3] = -1.0\n    return grad\n\ndef _constraints(x):\n    centers = x.reshape(N, 3)[:, :2]\n    radii = x[2::3]\n\n    boundary_constraints = np.empty(4 * N)\n    boundary_constraints[0*N : 1*N] = centers[:, 0] - radii  # x - r >= 0\n    boundary_constraints[1*N : 2*N] = 1.0 - (centers[:, 0] + radii) # 1 - x - r >= 0\n    boundary_constraints[2*N : 3*N] = centers[:, 1] - radii  # y - r >= 0\n    boundary_constraints[3*N\
    \ : 4*N] = 1.0 - (centers[:, 1] + radii) # 1 - y - r >= 0\n\n    dist_matrix = squareform(pdist(centers))\n    overlap_constraints = []\n    for i in range(N):\n        for j in range(i + 1, N):\n            overlap_constraints.append(dist_matrix[i, j] - (radii[i] + radii[j]))\n\n    return np.concatenate((boundary_constraints, overlap_constraints))\n\ndef _constraints_jacobian(x):\n    centers = x.reshape(N, 3)[:, :2]\n    radii = x[2::3]\n    grad = np.zeros((4 * N + N * (N - 1) // 2, N * 3))\n\n    for i in range(N):\n        grad[i, 3*i + 0] = 1.0; grad[i, 3*i + 2] = -1.0\n        grad[N + i, 3*i + 0] = -1.0; grad[N + i, 3*i + 2] = -1.0\n        grad[2*N + i, 3*i + 1] = 1.0; grad[2*N + i, 3*i + 2] = -1.0\n        grad[3*N + i, 3*i + 1] = -1.0; grad[3*N + i, 3*i + 2] = -1.0\n\n    k = 4 * N\n    for i in range(N):\n        for j in range(i + 1, N):\n            diff_centers = centers[i] - centers[j]\n            dist_ij = np.linalg.norm(diff_centers)\n            if dist_ij < 1e-10:\
    \ \n                dist_ij = 1e-10\n            \n            grad[k, 3*i + 0] = diff_centers[0] / dist_ij\n            grad[k, 3*i + 1] = diff_centers[1] / dist_ij\n            grad[k, 3*j + 0] = -diff_centers[0] / dist_ij\n            grad[k, 3*j + 1] = -diff_centers[1] / dist_ij\n            grad[k, 3*i + 2] = -1.0\n            grad[k, 3*j + 2] = -1.0\n            k += 1\n    return grad\n\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    # Load Scientia I's Nudged Packing (Eval ID 375) as base for multi-start\n    try:\n        base_centers = np.loadtxt(os.path.join(D_SCIENTIA_NUDGED_375_DATA_EXPORTED, 'centers.txt'))\n        base_radii = np.loadtxt(os.path.join(D_SCIENTIA_NUDGED_375_DATA_EXPORTED, 'radii.txt'))\n        print(f\"Loaded Scientia I Nudged (Eval ID 375) data from {D_SCIENTIA_NUDGED_375_DATA_EXPORTED}\")\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"Error loading Scientia I Nudged (Eval ID 375) data from {D_SCIENTIA_NUDGED_375_DATA_EXPORTED}: {e}. Falling back to a dense\
    \ grid for robustness.\")\n        base_centers = []\n        base_radii = []\n        radius = 0.08  \n        rows = 5\n        cols = 6\n        for i in range(rows):\n            for j in range(cols):\n                if len(base_centers) < N:\n                    x = 0.1 + i * 0.2\n                    y = 0.1 + j * 0.15\n                    base_centers.append([x, y])\n                    base_radii.append(radius)\n        base_centers = np.array(base_centers)\n        base_radii = np.array(base_radii)\n\n    base_centers, base_radii = make_feasible(base_centers, base_radii, eps=1e-8)\n\n    best_score = -np.sum(base_radii) # Negative sum of radii for minimization\n    best_centers = base_centers\n    best_radii = base_radii\n    total_restarts = 0\n\n    for jitter_mag in JITTER_AMPLITUDES:\n        for restart_idx in range(RESTARTS_PER_AMPLITUDE):\n            total_restarts += 1\n            # Apply perturbation to centers\n            current_centers = base_centers + np.random.uniform(-jitter_mag,\
    \ jitter_mag, base_centers.shape)\n            current_radii = base_radii \n\n            current_centers = np.clip(current_centers, R_MIN_CONSTRAINT, 1.0 - R_MIN_CONSTRAINT)\n            current_centers, current_radii = make_feasible(current_centers, current_radii, eps=1e-8)\n\n            initial_guess = np.zeros(N * 3)\n            initial_guess[0::3] = current_centers[:, 0]\n            initial_guess[1::3] = current_centers[:, 1]\n            initial_guess[2::3] = current_radii\n\n            lower_bounds = np.zeros(N * 3)\n            upper_bounds = np.ones(N * 3)\n            lower_bounds[2::3] = R_MIN_CONSTRAINT\n            upper_bounds[2::3] = 0.5\n\n            bounds = Bounds(lower_bounds, upper_bounds)\n            ineq_constraints = {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': _constraints, 'jac': _constraints_jacobian}\n\n            result = minimize(\n                _objective, \n                initial_guess,\n                method='SLSQP',\n                jac=_objective_jacobian, \n\
    \                bounds=bounds,\n                constraints=[ineq_constraints],\n                options={'maxiter': 500, 'ftol': 1e-10, 'disp': False} \n            )\n\n            if result.success and -result.fun > -best_score: \n                best_score = -result.fun\n                best_centers = result.x.reshape(N, 3)[:, :2]\n                best_radii = result.x[2::3]\n                best_centers, best_radii = make_feasible(best_centers, best_radii, eps=1e-8)\n                print(f\"Total Restart {total_restarts} (Jitter {jitter_mag:.0e}): New best score found: {-result.fun}\")\n            #else:\n                #print(f\"Total Restart {total_restarts} (Jitter {jitter_mag:.0e}): Score: {-result.fun if result.success else 'n.a.'} (Current best: {-best_score})\")\n\n    print(f\"Exhaustive local search finished. Best score: {-best_score}\")\n    return best_centers, best_radii\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nLoaded Scientia I Nudged\
    \ (Eval ID 375) data from storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/sota_nudged_375_data\nTotal Restart 1 (Jitter 1e-03): New best score found: 2.6359773947473504\nTotal Restart 2 (Jitter 1e-03): New best score found: 2.635977394752298\nTotal Restart 3 (Jitter 1e-03): New best score found: 2.6359773947536436\nTotal Restart 4 (Jitter 1e-03): New best score found: 2.6359773947539886\nTotal Restart 5 (Jitter 1e-03): New best score found: 2.6359773947503307\nTotal Restart 6 (Jitter 2e-03): New best score found: 2.6359773947535015\nTotal Restart 7 (Jitter 2e-03): New best score found: 2.6359773947544984\nTotal Restart 8 (Jitter 2e-03): New best score found: 2.635977394753889\nTotal Restart 9 (Jitter 2e-03): New best score found: 2.6359773947545637\nTotal Restart 10 (Jitter 2e-03): New best score found: 2.635977394734078\nTotal Restart 11 (Jitter 3e-03): New best score found: 2.6359773947566416\nTotal Restart 12 (Jitter 3e-03): New best score found: 2.635977394753024\nTotal Restart 13 (Jitter 3e-03): New\
    \ best score found: 2.6359773947499976\nTotal Restart 14 (Jitter 3e-03): New best score found: 2.6359773947546445\nTotal Restart 15 (Jitter 3e-03): New best score found: 2.63597739475302\nTotal Restart 16 (Jitter 4e-03): New best score found: 2.6359773947529064\nTotal Restart 17 (Jitter 4e-03): New best score found: 2.6359773947552054\nTotal Restart 18 (Jitter 4e-03): New best score found: 2.6359773947545864\nTotal Restart 19 (Jitter 4e-03): New best score found: 2.6359773947575067\nTotal Restart 20 (Jitter 4e-03): New best score found: 2.635977394754271\nTotal Restart 21 (Jitter 5e-03): New best score found: 2.6359773947602982\nTotal Restart 22 (Jitter 5e-03): New best score found: 2.6359773947292107\nTotal Restart 23 (Jitter 5e-03): New best score found: 2.6359773947568352\nTotal Restart 24 (Jitter 5e-03): New best score found: 2.635977394754302\nTotal Restart 25 (Jitter 5e-03): New best score found: 2.635977394761955\nTotal Restart 26 (Jitter 6e-03): New best score found: 2.635977394752564\n\
    Total Restart 27 (Jitter 6e-03): New best score found: 2.6359773947189664\nTotal Restart 28 (Jitter 6e-03): New best score found: 2.635977394755018\nTotal Restart 29 (Jitter 6e-03): New best score found: 2.6359773947176643\nTotal Restart 30 (Jitter 6e-03): New best score found: 2.63597739475631\nTotal Restart 31 (Jitter 7e-03): New best score found: 2.6359830849177897\nTotal Restart 32 (Jitter 7e-03): New best score found: 2.635977394753153\nTotal Restart 33 (Jitter 7e-03): New best score found: 2.635977394743709\nTotal Restart 34 (Jitter 7e-03): New best score found: 2.635983084935055\nTotal Restart 35 (Jitter 7e-03): New best score found: 2.6359773947484473\nTotal Restart 36 (Jitter 8e-03): New best score found: 2.635977394753587\nTotal Restart 37 (Jitter 8e-03): New best score found: 2.6359773947557175\nTotal Restart 38 (Jitter 8e-03): New best score found: 2.635977394756257\nTotal Restart 39 (Jitter 8e-03): New best score found: 2.635977394749822\nTotal Restart 40 (Jitter 8e-03):\
    \ New best score found: 2.635977394756083\nExhaustive local search finished. Best score: -2.635977394756083\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 416` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 416 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 418 | 1 | Utility: Jaccard Analysis of Scientia I Exhaustive Local Search Packing (Eval ID 416) vs All SOTA... | Scientia I | 249 | 2.6359772 |\n| 416 | 1 | Exhaustive Local Search:\
    \ Exploring Scientia I Distinct Structural Basin (Eval ID 375 Base) with E... | Scientia I | 248 | 2.6359772 |\n| 414 | 1 | Utility: Export Scientia I Nudged Packing (Eval ID 375) Data for Multi-Experiment Validation | Scientia I | 247 | 2.6359772 |\n| 409 | 1 | Exhaustive Local Search: Exploring Scientia I Distinct Structural Basin (Eval ID 375 Base) with E... | Scientia I | 245 | 2.6071967 |\n| 393 | 1 | Utility: Jaccard Analysis of Scientia I Nudged Packing (Eval ID 387) vs SOTAs & Previous Nudges -... | Scientia I | 233 | 2.6358955 |\n| 391 | 1 | Utility: Jaccard Analysis of Scientia I Nudged Packing (Eval ID 387) vs SOTAs & Previous Nudges -... | Scientia I | 232 | n.a. |\n| 389 | 1 | Utility: Jaccard Analysis of Scientia I Nudged Packing (Eval ID 387) vs SOTAs & Previous Nudges (... | Scientia I | 231 | n.a. |\n| 387 | 1 | Nudging Experiment 4: Local Multi-Start Optimization of Scientia I Nudged Packing (Eval ID 363) w... | Scientia I | 230 | 2.6358955 |\n| 384 | 1 | Utility: Export\
    \ Scientia I Nudged Packing (Eval ID 363) Data for Multi-Experiment Validation | Scientia I | 229 | 2.6351560 |\n| 379 | 1 | Nudging Experiment 4: Local Multi-Start Optimization of Scientia I Nudged Packing (Eval ID 363) w... | Scientia I | 227 | 2.5283696 |\n\nPage 1 of 8 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-8, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing\
    \ actions."
