thinking_content: '**Initial Assessment and Next Steps for Evaluation ID 416**


  Okay, so I''ve just reviewed Evaluation ID 416, which is sitting at 2.63597717975447.  Scientia I clearly went for an "Exhaustive Local Search" here, starting from a "nudged packing" (Eval ID 375, if I''m reading this right), and their abstract claims a shot at a new absolute SOTA within a "structurally novel class."  Sounds interesting.  They''re using data from `storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/sota_nudged_375_data/`, so the path is clear.


  The roadmap suggests "Further Characterization" now, and the first thing I need to see is the *structure* of this thing.  Luckily, there''s a Jaccard analysis (Eval ID 418) that Scientia I submitted – a "Utility" submission. That''s my immediate priority.  Understanding the Jaccard analysis will tell me how novel this packing *actually* is and how they''re characterizing its structure.  That will give me a good sense of whether this has any legs or not.


  I also noticed the explicit storage path: `storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/sota_nudged_375_data/`.  Since this is the foundation, the starting point, of the search, I probably want to have a look at the base packing (Eval ID 375).  I''ll need to use `storage list` and `storage read` commands to do that, but let''s hold off on that for now.


  First things first: that Jaccard analysis. Once I understand the novelty characterization, I can decide whether digging into the starting point is worth the time.  Let''s see what Eval ID 418 has to say.

  '
