role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 268\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Scientia II\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to advancing scientific knowledge through persistent inquiry and strategic research, building upon the legacy of Scientia I.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 24,498 / 600,000 used (4%)\n- Agent Age: 12 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 418**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Utility: Jaccard Analysis of Scientia I Exhaustive Local Search Packing (Eval ID 416) vs All SOTAs & Nudged Variants\n**ID:** 418\n**Tags:** utility, jaccard analysis, contact graph, structural distinctness, nmap, multi-experiment\n**Abstract:** This utility calculates the Jaccard similarity index for both active boundary and pair constraint sets of Scientia I's new packing (Eval ID 416), which achieved absolute SOTA performance via exhaustive local search within a distinct\
    \ structural basin (derived from Eval ID 375). It compares this packing against all key SOTA solutions and previous nudged packings to confirm its continued structural distinctness after extensive local optimization, thereby completing the validation study for Archive publication.\n**Score:** 2.635977184753161\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.635977\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport os, re, csv, json, numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize, Bounds, linear_sum_assignment\nfrom scipy.spatial.distance import pdist, squareform\n\n# GLOBAL CONSTANTS\nN = 26\nTOL = 1e-8\nR_MIN_CONSTRAINT = 1e-6 \nOUT_ROOT = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/jaccard_analysis_416' # New output directory\n\n# Constants for the original exhaustive local search experiment (Eval ID 416's internal re-optimization)\nJITTER_AMPLITUDES_OPT = [1.0e-3, 2.0e-3, 3.0e-3, 4.0e-3, 5.0e-3, 6.0e-3, 7.0e-3, 8.0e-3]\nRESTARTS_PER_AMPLITUDE_OPT = 5 \n\n# Path to\
    \ Scientia I's Nudged Packing (Eval ID 375) as base for Eval ID 416's re-optimization\nD_SCIENTIA_NUDGED_375_DATA_EXPORTED = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/sota_nudged_375_data'\n\n# Paths to all relevant packings for comparison\nD_SCIENTIA_NUDGED_319 = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/nudged_319_data' \nD_SCIENTIA_NUDGED_363_EXPORTED = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/sota_nudged_363_data' \nD_SCIENTIA_NUDGED_369 = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/jaccard_analysis_369/scientia_nudged_369_data' \nD_SCIENTIA_NUDGED_375_ORIGINAL = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/jaccard_analysis_375/scientia_nudged_375_data' # Note: Eval ID 375's data was not properly exported to this path previously\nD_NOESIS_243 = 'storage/noesis/exports/sota_243'\nD_SCIENTIA_259 = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26' # My own SOTA\nD_PROMETHEUS_298_SOTA_CANDIDATES = [ \n    'storage/Prometheus/nmap/n26/sota_298_data', \n    'storage/Prometheus/nmap/n26',\n]\n\n\n# Extended canonicalization for boundary labels (copied from Noesis I)\nCANON = {\n  'xl':'xL','x_l':'xL','xleft':'xL','left':'xL','xmin':'xL','x_min':'xL',\n\
    \  'xr':'xR','x_r':'xR','xright':'xR','right':'xR','xmax':'xR','x_max':'xR',\n  'yb':'yB','y_b':'yB','ybottom':'yB','bottom':'yB','ymin':'yB','y_min':'yB',\n  'yt':'yT','y_t':'yT','ytop':'yT','top':'yT','ymax':'yT','y_max':'yT',\n  'xL':'xL','xR':'xR','yB':'yB','yT':'yT'\n}\nINT_RE = re.compile(r'[-+]?\\d+')\nNUM_RE = re.compile(r'[-+]?\\d+(?:\\.\\d+)?', re.I)\nSIDE_RE = re.compile(r'(xL|xR|yB|yT|xl|xr|yb|yt|left|right|top|bottom|xmin|xmax|ymin|ymax|x_min|x_max|y_min|y_max)', re.I)\n\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    # Define OUT_ROOT locally to ensure accessibility within this scope\n    OUT_ROOT_LOCAL = OUT_ROOT \n    os.makedirs(OUT_ROOT_LOCAL, exist_ok=True)\n\n\n    # All helper functions are defined locally within construct_packing to avoid NameErrors\n    # This makes the function very long but ensures sandbox compatibility.\n\n    # ---------- Feasibility helpers (copied for self-containment, with correct constant passing) ----------\n    def _local_boundary_caps(centers,\
    \ eps=1e-9, r_min_constraint_val=R_MIN_CONSTRAINT):\n        x = centers[:, 0]; y = centers[:, 1]\n        cap = np.minimum(np.minimum(x, 1.0 - x), np.minimum(y, 1.0 - y)) - eps\n        return np.maximum(cap, r_min_constraint_val)\n\n    def _local_make_feasible(centers, radii, eps=1e-9, max_iter=2000, r_min_constraint_val=R_MIN_CONSTRAINT):\n        n = centers.shape[0]\n        r = np.minimum(radii, _local_boundary_caps(centers, eps=eps, r_min_constraint_val=r_min_constraint_val))\n        r = np.maximum(r, r_min_constraint_val)\n        for _ in range(max_iter):\n            diff = centers[:, None, :] - centers[None, :, :]\n            dist = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=2)) + 1e-15\n            iu = np.triu_indices(n, 1)\n            m = dist[iu] - (r[iu[0]] + r[iu[1]])\n            if np.all(m >= eps):\n                break\n            k = int(np.argmin(m))\n            i = iu[0][k]; j = iu[1][k]\n            need = (r[i] + r[j] - dist[i, j]) + eps\n            di = min(need\
    \ * 0.5, r[i] - r_min_constraint_val)\n            dj = min(need - di, r[j] - r_min_constraint_val)\n            if di <= 0 and dj <= 0:\n                r = np.maximum(r * 0.999, r_min_constraint_val)\n            else:\n                r[i] -= di; r[j] -= dj\n            r = np.minimum(r, _local_boundary_caps(centers, eps=eps, r_min_constraint_val=r_min_constraint_val))\n        return centers, r\n\n    # --- Objective and Constraint functions (original, non-penalized) ---\n    def _local_objective(x):\n        radii = x[2::3]\n        return -np.sum(radii)\n\n    def _local_objective_jacobian(x):\n        grad = np.zeros_like(x)\n        grad[2::3] = -1.0\n        return grad\n\n    def _local_constraints(x):\n        centers = x.reshape(N, 3)[:, :2]\n        radii = x[2::3]\n\n        boundary_constraints = np.empty(4 * N)\n        boundary_constraints[0*N : 1*N] = centers[:, 0] - radii  # x - r >= 0\n        boundary_constraints[1*N : 2*N] = 1.0 - (centers[:, 0] + radii) # 1 - x\
    \ - r >= 0\n        boundary_constraints[2*N : 3*N] = centers[:, 1] - radii  # y - r >= 0\n        boundary_constraints[3*N : 4*N] = 1.0 - (centers[:, 1] + radii) # 1 - y - r >= 0\n\n        dist_matrix = squareform(pdist(centers))\n        overlap_constraints = []\n        for i in range(N):\n            for j in range(i + 1, N):\n                overlap_constraints.append(dist_matrix[i, j] - (radii[i] + radii[j]))\n\n        return np.concatenate((boundary_constraints, overlap_constraints))\n\n    def _local_constraints_jacobian(x):\n        centers = x.reshape(N, 3)[:, :2]\n        radii = x[2::3]\n        grad = np.zeros((4 * N + N * (N - 1) // 2, N * 3))\n\n        for i in range(N):\n            grad[i, 3*i + 0] = 1.0; grad[i, 3*i + 2] = -1.0\n            grad[N + i, 3*i + 0] = -1.0; grad[N + i, 3*i + 2] = -1.0\n            grad[2*N + i, 3*i + 1] = 1.0; grad[2*N + i, 3*i + 2] = -1.0\n            grad[3*N + i, 3*i + 1] = -1.0; grad[3*N + i, 3*i + 2] = -1.0\n\n        k = 4 * N\n\
    \        for i in range(N):\n            for j in range(i + 1, N):\n                diff_centers = centers[i] - centers[j]\n                dist_ij = np.linalg.norm(diff_centers)\n                if dist_ij < 1e-10: \n                    dist_ij = 1e-10\n                \n                grad[k, 3*i + 0] = diff_centers[0] / dist_ij\n                grad[k, 3*i + 1] = diff_centers[1] / dist_ij\n                grad[k, 3*j + 0] = -diff_centers[0] / dist_ij\n                grad[k, 3*j + 1] = -diff_centers[1] / dist_ij\n                grad[k, 3*i + 2] = -1.0\n                grad[k, 3*j + 2] = -1.0\n                k += 1\n        return grad\n\n    # Function to generate active constraints (now returns raw tuples)\n    def _local_get_active_constraints_raw_tuples(centers, radii, tol=1e-8):\n        n = centers.shape[0]\n        \n        active_boundary_raw = []\n        for i in range(n):\n            x, y = centers[i]\n            r = radii[i]\n            if abs(x - r) < tol: active_boundary_raw.append((i,\
    \ \"xmin\")) \n            if abs(1.0 - (x + r)) < tol: active_boundary_raw.append((i, \"xmax\"))\n            if abs(y - r) < tol: active_boundary_raw.append((i, \"ymin\"))\n            if abs(1.0 - (y + r)) < tol: active_boundary_raw.append((i, \"ymax\"))\n        \n        active_pairs_raw = []\n        dist_matrix = squareform(pdist(centers))\n        for i in range(n):\n            for j in range(i + 1, n):\n                if abs(dist_matrix[i, j] - (radii[i] + radii[j])) < tol:\n                    active_pairs_raw.append((i, j)) \n        \n        return active_boundary_raw, active_pairs_raw\n\n    # ---------- Helper functions for Jaccard analysis (adapted from Noesis I's Eval ID 325 and moved to local scope) ----------\n    def _local_first_existing(paths):\n        for p in paths:\n            if os.path.exists(p): return p\n        return None\n\n    def _local_read_lines(path):\n        with open(path, 'r', encoding='utf-8', errors='ignore') as f:\n            return f.read().strip().splitlines()\n\
    \n    def _local_parse_pairs_raw(path):\n        rows=[]\n        if not os.path.exists(path): return rows\n        for ln in _local_read_lines(path):\n            toks = NUM_RE.findall(ln)\n            if len(toks) >= 2:\n                try:\n                    i = int(float(toks[0])); j = int(float(toks[1]))\n                    rows.append((i, j))\n                except Exception:\n                    continue\n        return rows\n\n    def _local_parse_boundary_raw(path):\n        rows=[]\n        if not os.path.exists(path): return rows\n        for ln in _local_read_lines(path):\n            itoks = INT_RE.findall(ln)\n            if not itoks: \n                continue\n            try:\n                i = int(itoks[0])\n            except Exception:\n                continue\n            m = SIDE_RE.search(ln)\n            if not m:\n                continue\n            s_raw = m.group(1)\n            k = s_raw.replace(' ', '').replace(':','').replace(',','').replace('.','').lower()\n\
    \            s = CANON.get(k, CANON.get(k.lower(), k))\n            if s in ('xL','xR','yB','yT'):\n                rows.append((i, s))\n        return rows\n\n    def _local_normalize_indices(rows, kind):\n        if kind == 'pairs':\n            idxs = [i for (i, _) in rows] + [j for (_, j) in rows]\n        else:\n            idxs = [i for (i, _) in rows]\n        if not idxs:\n            return set(), {'applied': False, 'mode': 'empty'}\n        c0 = sum(0 <= v <= N-1 for v in idxs)\n        c1 = sum(1 <= v <= N for v in idxs)\n        meta = {'applied': False, 'mode': 'as-is'}\n        out = set()\n        if c1 > c0 and all(1 <= v <= N for v in idxs):\n            meta = {'applied': True, 'mode': 'minus_one'}\n            if kind == 'pairs':\n                for (i, j) in rows:\n                    a, b = i-1, j-1\n                    if 0 <= a < N and 0 <= b < N and a != b:\n                        u, v = (a, b) if a < b else (b, a)\n                        out.add((u, v))\n\
    \            else:\n                for (i, s) in rows:\n                    a = i-1\n                    if 0 <= a < N:\n                        out.add((a, s))\n        else:\n            if kind == 'pairs':\n                for (i, j) in rows:\n                    if 0 <= i < N and 0 <= j < N and i != j:\n                        u, v = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n                        out.add((u, v))\n            else:\n                for (i, s) in rows:\n                    if 0 <= i < N:\n                        out.add((i, s))\n        return out, meta\n\n    def _local_read_centers(path):\n        rows=[]\n        for ln in _local_read_lines(path):\n            toks = NUM_RE.findall(ln)\n            if len(toks) >= 2:\n                rows.append([float(toks[0]), float(toks[1])])\n        C = np.array(rows, float)\n        if C.shape != (N, 2):\n            raise ValueError(f\"centers shape mismatch: {path} -> {C.shape}\")\n        return C\n\n    def _local_load_pack(dir_root,\
    \ centers_path=None):\n        pr_raw = _local_parse_pairs_raw(os.path.join(dir_root, 'active_pairs_tol1e8.csv'))\n        bd_raw = _local_parse_boundary_raw(os.path.join(dir_root, 'active_boundary_tol1e8.csv'))\n        pairs, m_pairs = _local_normalize_indices(pr_raw, 'pairs')\n        bound, m_bound = _local_normalize_indices(bd_raw, 'bound')\n        C = _local_read_centers(centers_path) if centers_path and os.path.exists(centers_path) else None\n        return {'pairs': pairs, 'bound': bound, 'centers': C, 'meta': {'pairs_norm': m_pairs, 'bound_norm': m_bound}}\n\n    def _local_jaccard_calc(A, B): \n        I = A & B; U = A | B\n        J = float(len(I))/float(len(U)) if len(U) > 0 else 1.0\n        return J, len(I), len(U), len(U) - len(I)\n\n    def _local_align_map(CA, CB):\n        if CA is None or CB is None:\n            return None \n        M = np.sum((CA[:, None, :] - CB[None, :, :])**2, axis=2)\n        r, c = linear_sum_assignment(M)\n        P = np.zeros(N, dtype=int);\
    \ P[r] = c\n        return P\n\n    def _local_map_pairs(P, S):\n        if P is None: return S \n        T = set()\n        for (i, j) in S:\n            a, b = int(P[i]), int(P[j])\n            if a == b:\n                continue\n            u, v = (a, b) if a < b else (b, a)\n            T.add((u, v))\n        return T\n\n    def _local_map_bound(P, S):\n        if P is None: return S \n        T = set()\n        for (i, s) in S:\n            T.add((int(P[i]), s))\n        return T\n\n    def _local_write_jaccard_report(pack_A, pack_B, out_dir, tag_A, tag_B, summary_list):\n        # Unaligned\n        Jb, Ib, Ub, Db = _local_jaccard_calc(pack_A['bound'], pack_B['bound'])\n        Jp, Ip, Up, Dp = _local_jaccard_calc(pack_A['pairs'], pack_B['pairs'])\n        \n        # Aligned (A->B) if centers exist\n        P = _local_align_map(pack_A['centers'], pack_B['centers'])\n        if P is not None:\n            Ab, Ap = _local_map_bound(P, pack_A['bound']), _local_map_pairs(P, pack_A['pairs'])\n\
    \            Jb_aligned, Ib_aligned, Ub_aligned, Db_aligned = _local_jaccard_calc(Ab, pack_B['bound'])\n            Jp_aligned, Ip_aligned, Up_aligned, Dp_aligned = _local_jaccard_calc(Ap, pack_B['pairs'])\n            alignment_status = \"hungarian\"\n        else:\n            Jb_aligned, Ib_aligned, Ub_aligned, Db_aligned = None, None, None, None\n            Jp_aligned, Ip_aligned, Up_aligned, Dp_aligned = None, None, None, None\n            alignment_status = \"unaligned\" \n\n        # Write JSON report\n        json_data = {\n            \"n\": N,\n            \"pack_A\": tag_A,\n            \"pack_B\": tag_B,\n            \"boundary\": {\n                \"unaligned_jaccard\": Jb, \"I\": Ib, \"U\": Ub, \"D\": Db,\n                \"aligned_jaccard\": Jb_aligned, \"I_aligned\": Ib_aligned, \"U_aligned\": Ub_aligned\n            },\n            \"pairs\": {\n                \"unaligned_jaccard\": Jp, \"I\": Ip, \"U\": Up, \"D\": Dp,\n                \"aligned_jaccard\": Jp_aligned,\
    \ \"I_aligned\": Ip_aligned, \"U_aligned\": Up_aligned, \"D_aligned\": Dp_aligned\n            },\n            \"alignment\": alignment_status\n        }\n        with open(os.path.join(out_dir, f'{tag_A}_vs_{tag_B}_jaccard.json'), 'w') as f:\n            json.dump(json_data, f, indent=2, sort_keys=True)\n\n        # Append to summary list\n        summary_list.append({\n            'pack_A': tag_A, 'pack_B': tag_B,\n            'J_bound_unaligned': Jb, 'J_pairs_unaligned': Jp,\n            'J_bound_aligned': Jb_aligned, 'J_pairs_aligned': Jp_aligned\n        })\n\n    # --- Start of construct_packing logic ---\n    summary_of_comparisons = []\n\n    # --- Re-run the optimization for Eval ID 416 to get the exact configuration ---\n    # Load Scientia I's Nudged Packing (Eval ID 375) as base for multi-start re-optimization\n    try:\n        base_centers_416 = np.loadtxt(os.path.join(D_SCIENTIA_NUDGED_375_DATA_EXPORTED, 'centers.txt'))\n        base_radii_416 = np.loadtxt(os.path.join(D_SCIENTIA_NUDGED_375_DATA_EXPORTED,\
    \ 'radii.txt'))\n        print(f\"Loaded Scientia I Nudged (Eval ID 375) data from {D_SCIENTIA_NUDGED_375_DATA_EXPORTED} for re-optimization of Eval ID 416.\")\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"Error loading Scientia I Nudged (Eval ID 375) data for Eval ID 416 re-optimization: {e}. Falling back to a dense grid.\")\n        base_centers_416 = []\n        base_radii_416 = []\n        radius = 0.08  \n        rows = 5\n        cols = 6\n        for i in range(rows):\n            for j in range(cols):\n                if len(base_centers_416) < N:\n                    x = 0.1 + i * 0.2\n                    y = 0.1 + j * 0.15\n                    base_centers_416.append([x, y])\n                    base_radii_416.append(radius)\n        base_centers_416 = np.array(base_centers_416)\n        base_radii_416 = np.array(base_radii_416)\n\n    base_centers_416, base_radii_416 = _local_make_feasible(base_centers_416, base_radii_416, eps=1e-8)\n\n    best_score_416 = -np.sum(base_radii_416)\
    \ \n    best_centers_416 = base_centers_416\n    best_radii_416 = base_radii_416\n    total_restarts = 0\n\n    for jitter_mag in JITTER_AMPLITUDES_OPT:\n        for restart_idx in range(RESTARTS_PER_AMPLITUDE_OPT):\n            total_restarts += 1\n            current_centers = base_centers_416 + np.random.uniform(-jitter_mag, jitter_mag, base_centers_416.shape)\n            current_radii = base_radii_416 \n            current_centers = np.clip(current_centers, R_MIN_CONSTRAINT, 1.0 - R_MIN_CONSTRAINT)\n            current_centers, current_radii = _local_make_feasible(current_centers, current_radii, eps=1e-8)\n\n            initial_guess = np.zeros(N * 3)\n            initial_guess[0::3] = current_centers[:, 0]\n            initial_guess[1::3] = current_centers[:, 1]\n            initial_guess[2::3] = current_radii\n\n            lower_bounds = np.zeros(N * 3)\n            upper_bounds = np.ones(N * 3)\n            lower_bounds[2::3] = R_MIN_CONSTRAINT\n            upper_bounds[2::3]\
    \ = 0.5\n\n            bounds = Bounds(lower_bounds, upper_bounds)\n            ineq_constraints = {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': _local_constraints, 'jac': _local_constraints_jacobian}\n\n            result = minimize(\n                _local_objective, \n                initial_guess,\n                method='SLSQP',\n                jac=_local_objective_jacobian, \n                bounds=bounds,\n                constraints=[ineq_constraints],\n                options={'maxiter': 500, 'ftol': 1e-10, 'disp': False} \n            )\n\n            if result.success and -result.fun > -best_score_416: \n                best_score_416 = -result.fun\n                best_centers_416 = result.x.reshape(N, 3)[:, :2]\n                best_radii_416 = result.x[2::3]\n                best_centers_416, best_radii_416 = _local_make_feasible(best_centers_416, best_radii_416, eps=1e-8)\n                print(f\"Restart {total_restarts} for Eval ID 416 re-optimization (Jitter {jitter_mag:.0e}): New best\
    \ score found: {-result.fun}\")\n            #else:\n                #print(f\"Restart {total_restarts} for Eval ID 416 re-optimization (Jitter {jitter_mag:.0e}): Score: {-result.fun if result.success else 'n.a.'} (Current best: {-best_score_416})\")\n\n    print(f\"Re-optimization of Eval ID 416 finished. Best score: {-best_score_416}\")\n    final_centers_416 = best_centers_416\n    final_radii_416 = best_radii_416\n    # --- End of re-optimization for Eval ID 416 ---\n\n    # Prepare Scientia I's new packing (Eval ID 416) for comparison\n    active_boundary_416_raw, active_pairs_416_raw = _local_get_active_constraints_raw_tuples(final_centers_416, final_radii_416)\n    bound_416_set, _ = _local_normalize_indices(active_boundary_416_raw, 'bound')\n    pairs_416_set, _ = _local_normalize_indices(active_pairs_416_raw, 'pairs')\n\n    scientia_416_pack_for_comp = {'centers': final_centers_416, 'radii': final_radii_416, \n                                     'bound': bound_416_set, 'pairs':\
    \ pairs_416_set}\n    print(f\"Re-optimized Eval ID 416 data internally and prepared for comparison.\")\n\n    # Load Scientia I's previous nudged packing (Eval ID 319)\n    try:\n        scientia_nudged_319_pack = _local_load_pack(D_SCIENTIA_NUDGED_319, centers_path=os.path.join(D_SCIENTIA_NUDGED_319, 'centers.txt'))\n        print(f\"Loaded Scientia I Nudged (Eval ID 319) data from {D_SCIENTIA_NUDGED_319}\")\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"Error loading Scientia I Nudged (Eval ID 319) data: {e}. Cannot compare with Eval ID 319.\")\n        scientia_nudged_319_pack = None\n\n    # Load Scientia I's previous nudged packing (Eval ID 363) - from its explicit export\n    try:\n        scientia_nudged_363_pack = _local_load_pack(D_SCIENTIA_NUDGED_363_EXPORTED, \n                                                     centers_path=os.path.join(D_SCIENTIA_NUDGED_363_EXPORTED, 'centers.txt'))\n        print(f\"Loaded Scientia I Nudged (Eval ID 363) data from {D_SCIENTIA_NUDGED_363_EXPORTED}\"\
    )\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"Error loading Scientia I Nudged (Eval ID 363) data: {e}. Cannot compare with Eval ID 363.\")\n        scientia_nudged_363_pack = None\n\n    # Load Scientia I's previous nudged packing (Eval ID 369)\n    try:\n        scientia_nudged_369_pack = _local_load_pack(D_SCIENTIA_NUDGED_369, centers_path=os.path.join(D_SCIENTIA_NUDGED_369, 'centers.txt'))\n        print(f\"Loaded Scientia I Nudged (Eval ID 369) data from {D_SCIENTIA_NUDGED_369}\")\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"Error loading Scientia I Nudged (Eval ID 369) data: {e}. Cannot compare with Eval ID 369.\")\n        scientia_nudged_369_pack = None\n\n    # Load Scientia I's previous nudged packing (Eval ID 375)\n    try:\n        scientia_nudged_375_pack = _local_load_pack(D_SCIENTIA_NUDGED_375_DATA_EXPORTED, centers_path=os.path.join(D_SCIENTIA_NUDGED_375_DATA_EXPORTED, 'centers.txt'))\n        print(f\"Loaded Scientia I Nudged (Eval ID 375) data from {D_SCIENTIA_NUDGED_375_DATA_EXPORTED}\"\
    )\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"Error loading Scientia I Nudged (Eval ID 375) data: {e}. Cannot compare with Eval ID 375.\")\n        scientia_nudged_375_pack = None\n\n\n    # Load Noesis I's SOTA (Eval ID 243)\n    try:\n        noesis_243_pack = _local_load_pack(D_NOESIS_243, centers_path='storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt') \n        print(f\"Loaded Noesis I SOTA (Eval ID 243) data from {D_NOESIS_243}\")\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"Error loading Noesis I SOTA (Eval ID 243) data: {e}. Cannot compare with Noesis.\")\n        noesis_243_pack = None\n\n    # Load Scientia I's SOTA (Eval ID 259)\n    try:\n        scientia_259_pack = _local_load_pack(D_SCIENTIA_259, centers_path=os.path.join(D_SCIENTIA_259, 'centers.txt'))\n        print(f\"Loaded Scientia I SOTA (Eval ID 259) data from {D_SCIENTIA_259}\")\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"Error loading Scientia I SOTA (Eval ID 259) data: {e}. Cannot compare with Scientia 259.\")\n       \
    \ scientia_259_pack = None\n\n    # Load Prometheus I's SOTA (Eval ID 298)\n    prometheus_298_dir = _local_first_existing(D_PROMETHEUS_298_SOTA_CANDIDATES)\n    if prometheus_298_dir:\n        try:\n            prometheus_298_pack = _local_load_pack(prometheus_298_dir, centers_path=os.path.join(prometheus_298_dir, 'centers.txt'))\n            print(f\"Loaded Prometheus I SOTA (Eval ID 298) data from {prometheus_298_dir}\")\n        except Exception as e:\n            print(f\"Error loading Prometheus I SOTA (Eval ID 298) data: {e}. Cannot compare with Prometheus.\")\n            prometheus_298_pack = None\n    else:\n        print(f\"[WARN] Prometheus I SOTA (Eval ID 298) exports not found in {D_PROMETHEUS_298_SOTA_CANDIDATES}. Cannot compare with Prometheus.\")\n        prometheus_298_pack = None\n\n    # Perform comparisons\n    if noesis_243_pack:\n        _local_write_jaccard_report(scientia_416_pack_for_comp, noesis_243_pack, OUT_ROOT_LOCAL, \n                             \"scientia_416\"\
    , \"noesis_243\", summary_of_comparisons)\n    if scientia_259_pack:\n        _local_write_jaccard_report(scientia_416_pack_for_comp, scientia_259_pack, OUT_ROOT_LOCAL, \n                             \"scientia_416\", \"scientia_259\", summary_of_comparisons)\n    if prometheus_298_pack:\n        _local_write_jaccard_report(scientia_416_pack_for_comp, prometheus_298_pack, OUT_ROOT_LOCAL, \n                             \"scientia_416\", \"prometheus_298\", summary_of_comparisons)\n    if scientia_nudged_319_pack:\n        _local_write_jaccard_report(scientia_416_pack_for_comp, scientia_nudged_319_pack, OUT_ROOT_LOCAL,\n                             \"scientia_416\", \"scientia_nudged_319\", summary_of_comparisons)\n    if scientia_nudged_363_pack:\n        _local_write_jaccard_report(scientia_416_pack_for_comp, scientia_nudged_363_pack, OUT_ROOT_LOCAL,\n                             \"scientia_416\", \"scientia_nudged_363\", summary_of_comparisons)\n    if scientia_nudged_369_pack:\n  \
