parts:
- text: "I have updated the `jaccard_calculator.py` script to include the necessary alignment logic. Now, I will submit a new utility evaluation to calculate the *aligned* Jaccard similarities between Scientia I's SOTA packing (Eval ID 416/375) and other SOTA packings. This will provide the quantitative verification of structural distinctness, as intended by Scientia I's roadmap.\n\nThis submission will load the centers, radii, and contact data for each packing, perform the alignment, and then calculate the aligned Jaccard similarities.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Utility: Aligned Jaccard Similarity Calculation for Comparative Structural Analysis\"\ntags: \"utility, jaccard similarity, contact graph, structural distinctness, N=26, quantitative analysis, alignment\"\nabstract: \"This utility calculates the ALIGNED Jaccard similarity indices for both active boundary and pair contact sets between Scientia I's absolute SOTA packing (Eval ID 416/375) and other prominent\
    \ N=26 SOTA packings (Scientia I (259), Noesis I (243), and Prometheus I (298)). It utilizes previously generated contact data and implements center-based alignment (Hungarian algorithm) to accurately validate structural distinctness, addressing a previous discrepancy with lineage findings.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import os\n  import sys\n\n  # Append the directory containing the utility script to sys.path\n  sys.path.append('storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/analysis')\n  from jaccard_calculator import _read_contact_file, jaccard_similarity\n\n  # Paths to Scientia I's SOTA (Eval ID 416/375)\n  S_SOTA_416_CENTERS = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/sota_nudged_375_data/centers.txt'\n  S_SOTA_416_RADII = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/sota_nudged_375_data/radii.txt'\n  S_SOTA_416_BOUNDARY_FILE = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/analysis_416/active_boundary_contacts.txt'\n  S_SOTA_416_PAIR_FILE = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/analysis_416/active_pair_contacts.txt'\n\n  # Paths to contact data for\
    \ other SOTAs (generated by Eval ID 459)\n  # Scientia I's SOTA (ID 259)\n  SCIENTIA_259_CENTERS = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/centers.txt'\n  SCIENTIA_259_RADII = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/radii.txt'\n  SCIENTIA_259_BOUNDARY_FILE = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/analysis_scientia_259/scientia_259_boundary_contacts.txt'\n  SCIENTIA_259_PAIR_FILE = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/analysis_scientia_259/scientia_259_pair_contacts.txt'\n\n  # Noesis I's SOTA (ID 243)\n  NOESIS_243_CENTERS = 'storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt'\n  NOESIS_243_RADII = 'storage/noesis/latest_radii.txt' \n  NOESIS_243_BOUNDARY_FILE = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/analysis_noesis_243/noesis_243_boundary_contacts.txt'\n  NOESIS_243_PAIR_FILE = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/analysis_noesis_243/noesis_243_pair_contacts.txt'\n\n  # Prometheus I's SOTA (ID 298) - Corrected path\n  PROMETHEUS_298_CENTERS = 'storage/Prometheus/nmap/n26/centers.txt'\n  PROMETHEUS_298_RADII = 'storage/Prometheus/nmap/n26/radii.txt'\n  PROMETHEUS_298_BOUNDARY_FILE\
    \ = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/analysis_prometheus_298/prometheus_298_boundary_contacts.txt'\n  PROMETHEUS_298_PAIR_FILE = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/analysis_prometheus_298/prometheus_298_pair_contacts.txt'\n\n  # Output directory for Jaccard results\n  JACCARD_RESULTS_DIR = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/jaccard_results_416_comparison_aligned'\n\n  N_CIRCLES = 26 # Fixed for this task\n\n  def _load_packing_data(centers_path, radii_path, boundary_file, pair_file, packing_name):\n      \"\"\"Helper to load all relevant packing data.\"\"\"\n      centers, radii, boundary_contacts, pair_contacts = None, None, set(), set()\n      try:\n          centers = np.loadtxt(centers_path)\n          radii = np.loadtxt(radii_path)\n          boundary_contacts = _read_contact_file(boundary_file)\n          pair_contacts = _read_contact_file(pair_file)\n          print(f\"Loaded all data for {packing_name}.\")\n          return centers, radii, boundary_contacts, pair_contacts\n      except Exception as\
    \ e:\n          print(f\"Error loading {packing_name} data: {e}. Skipping some comparisons.\")\n          return None, None, set(), set()\n\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      \"\"\"\n      Calculates and stores aligned Jaccard similarities between SOTA contact graphs.\n      \"\"\"\n      # Ensure Jaccard results directory exists\n      os.makedirs(JACCARD_RESULTS_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n      results_filepath = os.path.join(JACCARD_RESULTS_DIR, 'aligned_jaccard_comparison_summary.txt')\n\n      summary_lines = [\"Aligned Jaccard Similarity Comparison Results:\\n\"]\n\n      # Load data for Scientia I's SOTA (Eval ID 416/375)\n      s_416_centers, s_416_radii, s_416_boundary, s_416_pair = _load_packing_data(\n          S_SOTA_416_CENTERS, S_SOTA_416_RADII, S_SOTA_416_BOUNDARY_FILE, S_SOTA_416_PAIR_FILE, \"Scientia_SOTA_416_375\"\n      )\n      if s_416_centers is None:\n          print(\"Critical error: Failed to load Scientia_SOTA_416_375 data. Cannot proceed with comparisons.\"\
    )\n          # Return a trivial packing if critical data cannot be loaded\n          return np.array([[0.5, 0.5]] * N_CIRCLES), np.array([1e-3] * N_CIRCLES)\n      \n      print(f\"Loaded Scientia_SOTA_416_375 boundary contacts: {len(s_416_boundary)}, pair contacts: {len(s_416_pair)}\")\n\n\n      comparisons = [\n          (\"Scientia_259\", SCIENTIA_259_CENTERS, SCIENTIA_259_RADII, SCIENTIA_259_BOUNDARY_FILE, SCIENTIA_259_PAIR_FILE),\n          (\"Noesis_243\", NOESIS_243_CENTERS, NOESIS_243_RADII, NOESIS_243_BOUNDARY_FILE, NOESIS_243_PAIR_FILE),\n          (\"Prometheus_298\", PROMETHEUS_298_CENTERS, PROMETHEUS_298_RADII, PROMETHEUS_298_BOUNDARY_FILE, PROMETHEUS_298_PAIR_FILE),\n      ]\n\n      for name, centers_path, radii_path, boundary_file, pair_file in comparisons:\n          print(f\"\\n--- Comparing with {name} ---\")\n          other_centers, other_radii, other_boundary, other_pair = _load_packing_data(\n              centers_path, radii_path, boundary_file, pair_file, name\n\
    \          )\n\n          if other_centers is not None:\n              j_boundary_aligned = jaccard_similarity(s_416_boundary, other_boundary, s_416_centers, other_centers, aligned=True)\n              j_pair_aligned = jaccard_similarity(s_416_pair, other_pair, s_416_centers, other_centers, aligned=True)\n              \n              print(f\"Aligned Jaccard Boundary Similarity (416/375 vs {name}): {j_boundary_aligned:.4f}\")\n              print(f\"Aligned Jaccard Pair Similarity (416/375 vs {name}): {j_pair_aligned:.4f}\")\n\n              summary_lines.append(f\"Comparison: Scientia_SOTA_416_375 vs {name} (Aligned)\\n\")\n              summary_lines.append(f\"  Boundary Jaccard: {j_boundary_aligned:.4f}\\n\")\n              summary_lines.append(f\"  Pair Jaccard: {j_pair_aligned:.4f}\\n\")\n          else:\n              print(f\"Skipping aligned Jaccard calculation for {name} due to data loading issues.\")\n              summary_lines.append(f\"Comparison: Scientia_SOTA_416_375\
    \ vs {name} (Aligned) - Skipped due to data loading issues.\\n\")\n\n      # Write summary to a file\n      with open(results_filepath, 'w') as f:\n          f.writelines(summary_lines)\n      print(f\"\\nAligned Jaccard similarity analysis complete. Results saved to {results_filepath}\")\n\n      # Return the loaded 26-circle packing for evaluation\n      return s_416_centers, s_416_radii\n```"
