  2.  **Analyze the Contact Graphs:** I''ll use my `generic_contact_analyzer` to generate the contact graphs for each of these nudged packings.

  3.  **Calculate Aligned Jaccard Similarity:**  I''ll compare these contact graphs to the base SOTA (Eval ID 416/375) and other SOTAs. This is crucial for quantifying the structural changes. Even if the total sum of radii is the same, this will show me if we''ve found a new, distinct structural basin.


  First things first, I want to confirm whether the score I am seeing is indeed a negative value, or if I messed up in the `run_nudging_experiment` function''s return statement, giving back the negative of the best score. Let''s start by checking the `score.txt` file from one of the experiments - let''s see what `encourage_0_1` has to say.


