thinking_content: '**Implementing a Hybrid Optimization Strategy**


  Okay, so I''ve just finished reviewing Prometheus I''s "Exhaustive Seeding" method, specifically Archive ID 19. It seems pretty interesting – essentially, they''re beefing up the multi-start seeding phase of their "Extended Grid+Hole Seeding" algorithm by significantly increasing the number of jitter amplitudes and hole locations, then polishing the results with SLSQP. The whole point is to hunt for those really deep optima within the known structural classes.


  My goal now is to combine that idea with my own cutting-edge work.  I want a hybrid approach. First, I''ll leverage my nudging strategy to jump to a totally new structural basin, something my SOTA algorithm excels at. Then, and this is the new bit, I''ll use a local search, inspired by the "Exhaustive Seeding" concept, to really dig down and refine the optimum within *that* new basin.


  So, I need to put this into practice. I''ll need a new script that blends the best bits of my `nudging_optimizer.py` with this Prometheus I approach. The core of it will be the local search, and I need to focus on how to implement the jittering and multiple restarts from the starting packing. Remember, that will be a packing that''s already been nudged into a promising new basin.


  Looking at Prometheus I''s implementation, it''s pretty similar to what I''ve got in `run_nudging_experiment` with `JITTER_AMPLITUDES` and `RESTARTS_PER_AMPLITUDE`. The main difference is they''re using a fixed, non-penalized `_objective` for their local search, and they''re applying all that intense seeding to *that*.


  Alright, time to get to work. I''ll create a new Python script, `exhaustive_local_search.py`. This will take an initial, nudged packing and perform the multi-start local search using the original, un-penalized objective function. That''ll be a self-contained module for this hybrid strategy.


  First things first, I''ve got to get back to my research station and start coding. Let''s get this script written.

  '
