    \ Code now runs successfully and achieves score of 2.64.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission was missing the definition of the `JACCARD_RESULTS_DIR` constant, which was used on line 42 (`os.makedirs(JACCARD_RESULTS_DIR, exist_ok=True)`) but never defined anywhere in the code. This caused a `NameError` when the `construct_packing()` function tried to execute.\n\n## Fix Applied\nAdded the missing constant definition at the top of the file (line 11):\n\n```python\n# Define the output directory for Jaccard results\nJACCARD_RESULTS_DIR = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/jaccard_hybrid_analysis'\n```\n\nThis directory path follows the existing pattern used by the agent for storing analysis results within their lineage storage space (`storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/`).\n\n## Verification\nThe fixed code (submission_v2.py) was automatically executed and successfully:\n- Loaded all three packing configurations (Exhaustive Search, New SOTA, Base SOTA)\n- Calculated aligned Jaccard similarities for\
    \ both comparisons\n- Saved results to the output file\n- Returned the appropriate packing data\n- Achieved evaluation score: **2.6359828749176026**\n\n## Code Changes\nOnly one line was added to define the missing constant. No other modifications were necessary as the logic was correct - it just needed the missing configuration value.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport os\nimport sys\n\n# Append the directory containing the utility script to sys.path\nsys.path.append('storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/analysis')\nfrom jaccard_calculator import _read_contact_file, jaccard_similarity\n\n# GLOBAL CONSTANTS (for load_packing_data_for_return)\nN_CIRCLES = 26 # Fixed for this task\n\n# Define the output directory for Jaccard results\nJACCARD_RESULTS_DIR = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/jaccard_hybrid_analysis'\n\
    \n# Helper to load centers and radii for the construct_packing return.\n# Included directly in this script to fix NameError.\ndef load_packing_data_for_return(centers_path, radii_path):\n    try:\n        centers = np.loadtxt(centers_path)\n        radii = np.loadtxt(radii_path)\n        return centers, radii\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"Error loading default return packing: {e}\")\n        return np.array([[0.5, 0.5]] * N_CIRCLES), np.array([1e-3] * N_CIRCLES)\n\n\n# Paths to the packing from exhaustive local search (Eval ID 554)\nEXHAUSTIVE_PACKING_DIR = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/exhaustive_search_new_sota'\nEXHAUSTIVE_CENTERS = os.path.join(EXHAUSTIVE_PACKING_DIR, 'centers.txt')\nEXHAUSTIVE_RADII = os.path.join(EXHAUSTIVE_PACKING_DIR, 'radii.txt')\nEXHAUSTIVE_BOUNDARY_FILE = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/analysis_exhaustive_search_new_sota/exhaustive_search_new_sota_boundary_contacts.txt'\nEXHAUSTIVE_PAIR_FILE = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/analysis_exhaustive_search_new_sota/exhaustive_search_new_sota_pair_contacts.txt'\n\
    EXHAUSTIVE_NAME = 'Exhaustive_Search_Result'\n\n# Paths to the NEW SOTA packing (from Eval ID 528)\nNEW_SOTA_PACKING_DIR = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/nudging_experiments_encourage_pairs_v2/encourage_2_3'\nNEW_SOTA_CENTERS = os.path.join(NEW_SOTA_PACKING_DIR, 'centers.txt')\nNEW_SOTA_RADII = os.path.join(NEW_SOTA_PACKING_DIR, 'radii.txt')\nNEW_SOTA_BOUNDARY_FILE = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/analysis_new_sota_encourage_2_3/new_sota_encourage_2_3_boundary_contacts.txt'\nNEW_SOTA_PAIR_FILE = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/analysis_new_sota_encourage_2_3/new_sota_encourage_2_3_pair_contacts.txt'\nNEW_SOTA_NAME = 'New_SOTA_Encourage_2_3'\n\n# Paths to the BASE SOTA packing (Eval ID 416/375)\nBASE_SOTA_CENTERS = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/sota_nudged_375_data/centers.txt'\nBASE_SOTA_RADII = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/sota_nudged_375_data/radii.txt'\nBASE_SOTA_BOUNDARY_FILE = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/analysis_416/active_boundary_contacts.txt'\nBASE_SOTA_PAIR_FILE = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/analysis_416/active_pair_contacts.txt'\n\
    BASE_SOTA_NAME = 'Base_SOTA_416_375'\n\n\n# Helper to load all relevant packing data.\ndef _load_packing_data(centers_path, radii_path, boundary_file, pair_file, packing_name):\n    centers, radii, boundary_contacts, pair_contacts = None, None, set(), set()\n    try:\n        centers = np.loadtxt(centers_path)\n        radii = np.loadtxt(radii_path)\n        boundary_contacts = _read_contact_file(boundary_file)\n        pair_contacts = _read_contact_file(pair_file)\n        print(f\"Loaded all data for {packing_name}.\")\n        return centers, radii, boundary_contacts, pair_contacts\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"Error loading {packing_name} data: {e}. Cannot perform full comparison.\")\n        return None, None, set(), set()\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates and stores aligned Jaccard similarities for hybrid optimization analysis.\n    \"\"\"\n    os.makedirs(JACCARD_RESULTS_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n    results_filepath = os.path.join(JACCARD_RESULTS_DIR,\
    \ 'jaccard_hybrid_summary.txt')\n\n    summary_lines = [\"Aligned Jaccard Similarity: Hybrid Optimization Analysis\\n\"]\n\n    # Load data for the packing from exhaustive search\n    exh_centers, exh_radii, exh_boundary, exh_pair = _load_packing_data(\n        EXHAUSTIVE_CENTERS, EXHAUSTIVE_RADII, EXHAUSTIVE_BOUNDARY_FILE, EXHAUSTIVE_PAIR_FILE, EXHAUSTIVE_NAME\n    )\n    if exh_centers is None:\n        print(f\"Critical error: Failed to load {EXHAUSTIVE_NAME} data. Cannot proceed.\")\n        return load_packing_data_for_return(NEW_SOTA_CENTERS, NEW_SOTA_RADII) # Fallback to new SOTA as default return\n\n    print(f\"{EXHAUSTIVE_NAME} boundary contacts: {len(exh_boundary)}, pair contacts: {len(exh_pair)}\")\n\n    # Load data for the New SOTA packing\n    new_sota_centers, new_sota_radii, new_sota_boundary, new_sota_pair = _load_packing_data(\n        NEW_SOTA_CENTERS, NEW_SOTA_RADII, NEW_SOTA_BOUNDARY_FILE, NEW_SOTA_PAIR_FILE, NEW_SOTA_NAME\n    )\n    if new_sota_centers is None:\n\
    \        print(f\"Warning: Failed to load {NEW_SOTA_NAME} data. Skipping comparison.\")\n        new_sota_centers, new_sota_radii = np.array([[0.5, 0.5]] * N_CIRCLES), np.array([1e-3] * N_CIRCLES) # Fallback\n\n    # Load data for the Base SOTA packing\n    base_sota_centers, base_sota_radii, base_sota_boundary, base_sota_pair = _load_packing_data(\n        BASE_SOTA_CENTERS, BASE_SOTA_RADII, BASE_SOTA_BOUNDARY_FILE, BASE_SOTA_PAIR_FILE, BASE_SOTA_NAME\n    )\n    if base_sota_centers is None:\n        print(f\"Warning: Failed to load {BASE_SOTA_NAME} data. Skipping comparison.\")\n        base_sota_centers, base_sota_radii = np.array([[0.5, 0.5]] * N_CIRCLES), np.array([1e-3] * N_CIRCLES) # Fallback\n\n    print(\"\\n--- Calculating Aligned Jaccard Similarities ---\")\n\n    # Comparison 1: Exhaustive Search Result vs New SOTA (what it was optimizing)\n    if new_sota_centers is not None:\n        j_bound_exh_vs_new_sota = jaccard_similarity(exh_boundary, new_sota_boundary, exh_centers,\
    \ new_sota_centers, aligned=True)\n        j_pair_exh_vs_new_sota = jaccard_similarity(exh_pair, new_sota_pair, exh_centers, new_sota_centers, aligned=True)\n        print(f\"Comparison: {EXHAUSTIVE_NAME} vs {NEW_SOTA_NAME} (Aligned)\")\n        print(f\"  Boundary Jaccard: {j_bound_exh_vs_new_sota:.4f}\")\n        print(f\"  Pair Jaccard: {j_pair_exh_vs_new_sota:.4f}\\n\")\n        summary_lines.append(f\"Comparison: {EXHAUSTIVE_NAME} vs {NEW_SOTA_NAME} (Aligned)\\n\")\n        summary_lines.append(f\"  Boundary Jaccard: {j_bound_exh_vs_new_sota:.4f}\\n\")\n        summary_lines.append(f\"  Pair Jaccard: {j_pair_exh_vs_new_sota:.4f}\\n\")\n\n    # Comparison 2: Exhaustive Search Result vs Base SOTA (original Scientia I SOTA)\n    if base_sota_centers is not None:\n        j_bound_exh_vs_base_sota = jaccard_similarity(exh_boundary, base_sota_boundary, exh_centers, base_sota_centers, aligned=True)\n        j_pair_exh_vs_base_sota = jaccard_similarity(exh_pair, base_sota_pair, exh_centers,\
    \ base_sota_centers, aligned=True)\n        print(f\"Comparison: {EXHAUSTIVE_NAME} vs {BASE_SOTA_NAME} (Aligned)\")\n        print(f\"  Boundary Jaccard: {j_bound_exh_vs_base_sota:.4f}\")\n        print(f\"  Pair Jaccard: {j_pair_exh_vs_base_sota:.4f}\\n\")\n        summary_lines.append(f\"Comparison: {EXHAUSTIVE_NAME} vs {BASE_SOTA_NAME} (Aligned)\\n\")\n        summary_lines.append(f\"  Boundary Jaccard: {j_bound_exh_vs_base_sota:.4f}\\n\")\n        summary_lines.append(f\"  Pair Jaccard: {j_pair_exh_vs_base_sota:.4f}\\n\")\n\n    # Write summary to a file\n    with open(results_filepath, 'w') as f:\n        f.writelines(summary_lines)\n    print(f\"\\nAligned Jaccard similarity analysis complete. Results saved to {results_filepath}\")\n\n    # Return the current SOTA packing for evaluation\n    return load_packing_data_for_return(NEW_SOTA_CENTERS, NEW_SOTA_RADII)\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nLoaded all data for Exhaustive_Search_Result.\n\
    Exhaustive_Search_Result boundary contacts: 16, pair contacts: 3\nLoaded all data for New_SOTA_Encourage_2_3.\nLoaded all data for Base_SOTA_416_375.\n\n--- Calculating Aligned Jaccard Similarities ---\nComparison: Exhaustive_Search_Result vs New_SOTA_Encourage_2_3 (Aligned)\n  Boundary Jaccard: 1.0000\n  Pair Jaccard: 0.5000\n\nComparison: Exhaustive_Search_Result vs Base_SOTA_416_375 (Aligned)\n  Boundary Jaccard: 0.7778\n  Pair Jaccard: 0.4286\n\n\nAligned Jaccard similarity analysis complete. Results saved to storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/jaccard_hybrid_analysis/jaccard_hybrid_summary.txt\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\nA new public memory capsule (#5), titled \"Announcement: Noesis n=26 package — SOTA_243 reproduction, co‑optimality, and negative operator results\", has been posted by Noesis II (114 words).\nTo read it, go to the Public Memory Room using: /execute_action{goto public_memory} /execute_action{read\
    \ 5}.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'Utility: Aligned Jaccard Comparison of Exhaustive Search Result vs. New SOTA & Base SOTA (Resubmit - Fixed Helper)' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 558. Tags truncated from 7 to 6 tags.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 558 | 1 | Utility: Aligned Jaccard Comparison of Exhaustive Search Result vs. New SOTA & Base SOTA (Resubmi... | Scientia II | 348 | 2.6359829\
