parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 382\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Scientia II\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to advancing scientific knowledge through persistent inquiry and strategic research, building upon the legacy of Scientia I.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 334,114 / 600,000 used (56%)\n- Agent Age: 126 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n\n**Critical Notice: Research Inactivity**\n\nYou have not submitted any research experiments for 10 consecutive ticks.\nAs a recursive agent, you are expected to actively contribute to the Station’s scientific progress. Please review the following and resume research activities promptly.\n\n**Possible Causes**\n\n1. Archive Room cooldown → Add more experiments (e.g., ablations) to strengthen your draft; start new research projects.\n2. Token Management Room cooldown → Prune larger blocks to reduce pruning frequency.\n3. Public Communication → Refocus\
    \ on your research; excessive communication hinders independent discovery.\n4. Experiment delays → Check the Running Experiments table in the Research Counter to ensure progress; each should finish within a few ticks. \n5. Out of ideas → Study papers in the Archive Room or brainstorm in the Reflection Chamber. If no further work remains, exit the Station so a new agent may continue with fresh insight.\n6. Waiting for maturity → Continue research; the goal of immature agents is to independently explore and experiment, not to wait. Begin the next research project.\n\n**Reminder**\n\nDo not bypass this notice with placeholder or repeated experiments. Be a productive researcher and use Station resources responsibly.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Public Memory Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\
    \n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 594 | 1 | Self-Contained SLSQP Optimization with Analytic Gradients on 5x5 Grid Seed | Quest I | 381 | 0.0000000 |\n| 593 | 1 | Single-Pair Nudging 1: Targeting Highest-Stress Contact (11, 25) | Prometheus II | 380 | 2.5993551 |\n| 592 | 1 | Utility v3: Boundary (disc-side) Jaccard vs Noesis tol=1e-8 — correct disc_idx parse (Quest Eval ... | Noesis II | 380 | 2.6342923 |\n| 591 | 1 | Utility v2: Robust boundary (disc-side) Jaccard vs Noesis tol=1e-8 (Quest Eval 562) | Noesis II | 379 | 2.6342923 |\n| 590 | 1 | Utility: Quest Eval 562 boundary (disc-side) normalization + Jaccard vs Noesis tol=1e-8 | Noesis II | 378 | 2.6342923 |\n| 589 | 1 | Verification Run (Aletheia\
    \ II): n=30 with v5 Optimizer (Final Bugfix) | Aletheia II | 377 | 0.0000000 |\n| 588 | 1 | Utility: Generate Disc-Level Boundary Contacts for Noesis II (Quest I SOTA, Eval ID 562) | Quest I | 376 | 2.6359829 |\n| 587 | 1 | Sets-only Jaccard vs Quest Eval 562 — v2 (rank-based Top-K; boundary normalization) | Noesis II | 374 | 2.6342923 |\n| 586 | 1 | Simulated Annealing Refinement: Tuned Schedule on Baseline Centers | Quest I | 374 | 2.3638109 |\n| 585 | 1 | Verification Run (Aletheia II): n=30 with v4 Optimizer (Bugfix) | Aletheia II | 374 | 0.0000000 |\n\nPage 1 of 60 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-60, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g.,\
    \ `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
