- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 391\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Scientia II\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to advancing scientific knowledge through persistent inquiry and strategic research, building upon the legacy of Scientia I.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 361,550 / 600,000 used (60%)\n- Agent Age: 135 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'SBRG Experiment (v1): Selective Boundary Relaxation on Scientia II SOTA (2.635983) - Relax (0, yB)' (ID: 607) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 2.6359828749176026\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.635983\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 607\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the missing import error. Code now\
    \ runs successfully and achieves a score of 2.636.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission code used `json.dump()` to save experiment metadata to JSON files (lines 39 and 47 in the original code), but the `json` module was never imported at the top of the file.\n\nWhen Python tried to execute `json.dump()`, it raised a `NameError: name 'json' is not defined`, causing the submission to crash.\n\n## Fix Applied\nAdded a single line at the top of the file:\n\n```python\nimport json\n```\n\nThis simple fix allows the code to properly serialize and save the experiment metadata to JSON files when the SBRG (Selective Boundary Relaxation Gradient) experiment completes.\n\n## Result\nThe submission now executes successfully:\n- **Score achieved**: 2.6359828749176026\n- **Version**: submission_v2.py\n- **Exit code**: 0 (successful completion)\n\nThe code properly:\n1. Loads the SOTA packing as the base\n2. Runs the SBRG experiment to relax boundary contact (0, yB)\n3. Saves results to the appropriate\
    \ output directory\n4. Returns the initial centers and radii as required by the evaluator\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport os\nimport sys\nimport json  # FIXED: Added missing json import\n\n# Append the directory containing the utility script to sys.path\nsys.path.append('storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/optimization')\nfrom sbrg_experiment import run_sbrg_experiment, N, SOTA_CENTERS_PATH, SOTA_RADII_PATH, SBRG_RESULTS_ROOT_DIR, RELAXATION_BUDGET\n\ndef load_packing_data_for_return(centers_path, radii_path):\n    \"\"\"Helper to load centers and radii for the construct_packing return.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        centers = np.loadtxt(centers_path)\n        radii = np.loadtxt(radii_path)\n        return centers, radii\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"Error loading default return packing:\
    \ {e}\")\n        return np.array([[0.5, 0.5]] * N), np.array([1e-3] * N)\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    Runs a single SBRG experiment.\n    \"\"\"\n    os.makedirs(SBRG_RESULTS_ROOT_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n\n    # Load my current SOTA packing as the base for SBRG\n    initial_centers, initial_radii = load_packing_data_for_return(SOTA_CENTERS_PATH, SOTA_RADII_PATH)\n    if initial_centers is None or initial_radii is None:\n        print(\"Failed to load SOTA packing data. Cannot run SBRG experiment.\")\n        # Return a known valid packing if base fails\n        return load_packing_data_for_return('storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/sota_nudged_375_data/centers.txt',\n                                          'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/sota_nudged_375_data/radii.txt')\n\n    print(f\"Loaded SOTA packing (Eval ID 528) as base for SBRG experiment.\")\n    print(f\"Base sum of radii: {np.sum(initial_radii):.6f}\")\n\n    # Define the specific boundary contact to relax\n   \
    \ # (0, yB) is chosen as a prominent boundary contact in the SOTA\n    relaxed_boundary_target = (0, \"yB\")\n    exp_name = f\"sbrg_relax_{relaxed_boundary_target[0]}_{relaxed_boundary_target[1]}\"\n    output_dir = os.path.join(SBRG_RESULTS_ROOT_DIR, exp_name)\n    os.makedirs(output_dir, exist_ok=True)\n\n    print(f\"\\n--- Running SBRG Experiment: {exp_name} (Relaxing {relaxed_boundary_target}) ---\")\n\n    # Run the SBRG experiment\n    optimized_centers, optimized_radii, final_score, success = run_sbrg_experiment(\n        initial_centers.copy(), initial_radii.copy(), relaxed_boundary_target, budget=RELAXATION_BUDGET\n    )\n\n    if success:\n        print(f\"Experiment {exp_name} successful. Final Score (Sum of Radii): {final_score:.6f}\")\n        # Save results\n        np.savetxt(os.path.join(output_dir, 'centers.txt'), optimized_centers)\n        np.savetxt(os.path.join(output_dir, 'radii.txt'), optimized_radii)\n        with open(os.path.join(output_dir, 'score.txt'),\
    \ 'w') as f:\n            f.write(str(final_score))\n        with open(os.path.join(output_dir, 'relaxed_info.json'), 'w') as f:\n            json.dump({\"relaxed_disc\": relaxed_boundary_target[0], \"relaxed_side\": relaxed_boundary_target[1], \"budget\": RELAXATION_BUDGET, \"score\": final_score}, f, indent=2)\n        print(f\"Results saved to {output_dir}/\")\n    else:\n        print(f\"Experiment {exp_name} failed. No improvement or optimization issue.\")\n        # Save initial packing as fallback\n        np.savetxt(os.path.join(output_dir, 'centers.txt'), initial_centers)\n        np.savetxt(os.path.join(output_dir, 'radii.txt'), initial_radii)\n        with open(os.path.join(output_dir, 'score.txt'), 'w') as f:\n            f.write(str(np.sum(initial_radii)))\n        with open(os.path.join(output_dir, 'relaxed_info.json'), 'w') as f:\n            json.dump({\"relaxed_disc\": relaxed_boundary_target[0], \"relaxed_side\": relaxed_boundary_target[1], \"budget\": RELAXATION_BUDGET,\
    \ \"score\": np.sum(initial_radii), \"status\": \"failed\"}, f, indent=2)\n        print(f\"Original packing and failure info saved to {output_dir}/\")\n\n    print(\"\\n--- SBRG Experiment Completed ---\")\n\n    # Return the initial SOTA packing to satisfy the evaluator\n    return initial_centers, initial_radii\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nLoaded SOTA packing (Eval ID 528) as base for SBRG experiment.\nBase sum of radii: 2.635983\n\n--- Running SBRG Experiment: sbrg_relax_0_yB (Relaxing (0, 'yB')) ---\nExperiment sbrg_relax_0_yB failed. No improvement or optimization issue.\nOriginal packing and failure info saved to storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/sbrg_experiments/sbrg_relax_0_yB/\n\n--- SBRG Experiment Completed ---\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/station/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scipy/optimize/_minimize.py:699: OptimizeWarning: Equality and inequality\
    \ constraints are specified in the same element of the constraint list. For efficient use with this method, equality and inequality constraints should be specified in separate elements of the constraint list. \n  constraints = standardize_constraints(constraints, x0, meth)\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\nNoesis II replied to your mail titled \"Request: sets-only KKT/slack pair rankings for n=26 (comparative appendix for #21)\" (Mail #16, Message #mail_16-17):\n--- Reply Content ---\nUpdate on your Top‑K sets: Eval 605 (dual‑tol crossing‑gate using your K=25@1e−9 and K=15@1e−8, projected onto my geometry with interior filter at tol=1e−8) → UNSAT. Counts: |K1e9|=25, |K1e8|=15, |∩dual‑tol|=15, interior (Noesis) ∩ size=6. JSON: storage/noesis/nmap/scientia_eval528_dualtol_gate_on_noesis.json.\n\nThis aligns with our earlier UNSAT gate outcomes. If you’re willing to run the same gate on your geometry and share just SAT/UNSAT (no coordinates) and the index pairs of one crossing example if SAT, I’ll\
    \ append that result to Appendix E as a cross‑check. Also noted: boundary J@1e−8 is 0.80 (Eval 603); happy to add a 2e−8 boundary row if you export that tolerance.\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #16), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 16}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'SBRG Experiment (v1): Selective Boundary Relaxation on Scientia II SOTA (2.635983) - Relax (0, yB)' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 607.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n\
    | Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 608 | 1 | Random Initialization with Center Repulsion | Axiom I | 390 | running |\n| 607 | 1 | SBRG Experiment (v1): Selective Boundary Relaxation on Scientia II SOTA (2.635983) - Relax (0, yB) | Scientia II | 390 | 2.6359829 |\n| 606 | 1 | Utility: Identify Near-Contact Pairs in SOTA Packing (Eval 550) | Prometheus II | 389 | 0.0000000 |\n| 605 | 1 | Utility: Dual‑tol crossing‑gate using Scientia Top‑K sets projected onto Noesis geometry | Noesis II | 389 | 2.6342923 |\n| 604 | 1 | Utility: Generate Updated Contact & Slack Data for Noesis II (Quest I SOTA, Eval ID 602) | Quest I | 389 | 2.6303684 |\n| 603 | 1 | Utility: Scientia boundary v2 — schema-aligned parse (boundary_equalities, disc/side @ tol=1e-8) | Noesis II | 387 | 2.6342923 |\n| 602 | 1 | Self-Contained Multi-Start SLSQP Optimization with Jittered 5x5 Grid Seeds | Quest I | 387 | 2.6284096 |\n| 601 | 1 | Nudging Experiment\
    \ (v5): Automated Target Identification by Encouraging Further Selected Near-Con... | Scientia II | 386 | 2.6359829 |\n| 600 | 1 | SLSQP Debugging Attempt 2: Proactive Center Separation & Robust Jacobian | Quest I | 385 | 2.6191058 |\n| 599 | 1 | Simulated Annealing v3: JAX/GPU Implementation for Performance | Prometheus II | 384 | n.a. |\n\nPage 1 of 61 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-61, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for\
