- text: "I am in the Token Management Room. I am pruning my dialogue history to optimize my token budget, which is currently at 79%. I have carefully selected several blocks of past ticks to prune, providing concise but information-complete summaries to maintain context for future operations.\n\n`/execute_action{prune_response}`\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"256-263\"\n    summary: \"Agent Guest_8 read Codex, passed promotion test, and ascended to Scientia II. Read Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square.\"\n  - ticks: \"265-285\"\n    summary: \"Reviewed Scientia I's SOTA (Eval ID 416, 418) and performed initial contact graph analysis (Eval ID 447). Conducted initial, unaligned Jaccard comparisons (Eval ID 456, 459). Read Private Memory Capsules 2 & 3. Created and refined Private Memory Capsule 4 (initial characterization of SOTA). Mail exchanges with Prometheus I and Noesis II.\"\n  - ticks: \"286-305\"\n    summary: \"Refined Jaccard calculation with alignment (Eval ID\
    \ 466, 471). Visualized contact graphs (Eval ID 480). Conducted initial nudging attempts (discouraging contacts) which failed (Eval ID 482, 484). Updated PM Capsule 4 with aligned Jaccard results and discrepancy analysis. Read Inquire I's foundational nudging paper (Archive ID 13). Updated `nudging_optimizer.py` to include encouragement. Identified near-contact pairs (Eval ID 498). Ran Batch 1 nudging (encouraging contacts, Eval ID 502) and analyzed its structural outcome (Eval ID 508, 510). Attempted SBRG experiments v1 & v2 (Eval ID 607, 611) which failed.\"\n  - ticks: \"306-322\"\n    summary: \"Maturity achieved. Reviewed Archive ID 13. Updated `nudging_optimizer.py` with encouragement. Identified near-contact pairs (Eval ID 498). Ran Nudging Batch 1 (Eval ID 502) and structural analysis (Eval ID 508, 510). Mail exchanges with Prometheus I and Noesis II. Attempted SBRG experiments v1 & v2 (Eval ID 607, 611) which failed.\"\n  - ticks: \"323-336\"\n    summary: \"Ran Nudging Batch\
    \ 2 (Eval ID 528) and discovered new SOTA `encourage_2_3`. Performed contact graph (Eval ID 532) and Jaccard analysis (Eval ID 535) for new SOTA. Drafted Archive paper for new SOTA (Capsule 5). Successfully published Archive ID 20.\"\n  - ticks: \"337-353\"\n    summary: \"Read Archive ID 19 (Prometheus I's exhaustive seeding). Created `exhaustive_local_search.py`. Ran exhaustive search on `encourage_2_3` (Eval ID 554). Analyzed result (Eval ID 556, 558). Mail exchanges with Noesis II. Read Archive ID 21 (Noesis II's paper). Updated PM Capsule 4 with new insights.\"\n  - ticks: \"354-381\"\n    summary: \"Ran Nudging Batch 3 (Eval ID 565), analyzed `encourage_1_2` (Eval ID 566, 567). Ran Nudging Batch 4 (Eval ID 576), discovered `encourage_1_7` (new SOTA). Analyzed `encourage_1_7` (Eval ID 578, 581). Ran Nudging Batch 5 (Eval ID 601). Updated PM Capsule 4 with results and Quest I insights (Archive ID 22). Read Public Memory Capsule 5 (Noesis II updates).\"\n  - ticks: \"382-412\"\n \
    \   summary: \"Exported Scientia II SOTA contact data for Noesis II (Eval ID 596, 615). Ran dual-tolerance crossing-gate on Scientia II SOTA (Eval ID 623), result SAT. Ran Nudging Batch 6 (Eval ID 641), discovered `encourage_3_9` (new SOTA structural class). Analyzed `encourage_3_9` (Eval ID 645, 648). Mail exchanges with Noesis II. Documented Hybrid Strategy in Capsule 6.\"\n  - ticks: \"413-431\"\n    summary: \"Drafted Archive paper for new SOTA structural class (Capsule 7). Successfully published Archive ID 23. Applied Exhaustive Search to `encourage_3_9` (Eval ID 665). Analyzed result (Eval ID 666). Ran Nudging Batch 7 (Eval ID 673), discovered `encourage_8_14` (another new SOTA structural class). Analyzed `encourage_8_14` (Eval ID 675, 678). Updated PM Capsule 4. Drafted Archive paper for multiple SOTA structural classes (Capsule 8). Mail exchanges with Noesis II (Mail #22, #23, #24).\"\n```"
thinking_content: '**My Pruning Strategy**


  I''m currently at 79% token usage and need to prune my dialogue history effectively. The goal is to remove substantial portions while preserving enough context to continue my research seamlessly. I''ve broken down my historical dialogue into several blocks for efficient pruning.


  Here''s my plan:


  *   **Block 1 (Ticks 256-263):** This block covers my initial setup phase: becoming a recursive agent and reading the Codex. This is well-covered in my private memory, so it''s safe to prune.

  *   **Block 2 (Ticks 265-285):** This involves the initial analysis of Scientia I''s SOTA and comparisons using the Jaccard index.  I''ve created a private memory capsule for this, making this block redundant.

  *   **Block 3 (Ticks 286-305):** Focuses on the failures of my initial attempts to nudge the system and SBRG experiments. This is also well-documented in my private memory.

  *   **Block 4 (Ticks 306-322):** This includes the initial Nudging Batch, failures in SBGR and communications, again documented in memory.

  *   **Block 5 (Ticks 323-336):** My discovery of the first new SOTA, `encourage_2_3`. This is thoroughly covered in my capsule and Archive ID 20.

  *   **Block 6 (Ticks 337-353):** This includes my work with exhaustive search and the reading of another paper. This also exists elsewhere.

  *   **Block 7 (Ticks 354-381):** Includes the Nudging and creation of a new SOTA. This is fully summarized in Private Memory and Archive information.

  *   **Block 8 (Ticks 382-412):** All the data export and discovery of structural classes. This information now exists in a specific location.

  *   **Block 9 (Ticks 413-422):** The publication of Archive ID 23 and work on more exhaustive searches.

  *   **Block 10 (Ticks 423-431):** The work is all documented elsewhere as well.


  I will execute the pruning based on these defined blocks. My intention is to maintain a coherent and useful history while freeing up the necessary tokens.

  '
