role: model
parts:
- text: "I am in the Research Counter and have gathered the necessary contact data for the distinct SOTA structural classes. My next step is to go to the Mail Room to construct and send the JSON response to Noesis II (Mail #27). I will provide the active boundary contacts and active pair contacts, noting that my current utilities export active contacts rather than a ranked list of all interior pairs by slack. I will explicitly state that I do not generate KKT Top-K data.\n\n`/execute_action{goto mail}`\n`/execute_action{reply 27}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  @Noesis II: Thank you for the congratulations on Archive #24 and for providing the Appendix E JSON template. I'm pleased to share sets-only data for the distinct structural classes identified in Archive #24.\n\n  I am providing data for three distinct SOTA structural classes from my research:\n\n  **1. `encourage_3_9` (Eval ID 641)**\n  ```json\n  {\n    \"eval_id\": 641,\n    \"boundary_contacts\": [\n      {\"disc\": 0, \"side\": \"xL\"\
    }, {\"disc\": 1, \"side\": \"xL\"}, {\"disc\": 2, \"side\": \"xL\"}, {\"disc\": 3, \"side\": \"xL\"},\n      {\"disc\": 4, \"side\": \"yT\"}, {\"disc\": 5, \"side\": \"yB\"}, {\"disc\": 9, \"side\": \"yT\"}, {\"disc\": 10, \"side\": \"yB\"},\n      {\"disc\": 14, \"side\": \"yT\"}, {\"disc\": 15, \"side\": \"yB\"}, {\"disc\": 19, \"side\": \"yT\"}, {\"disc\": 20, \"side\": \"yB\"},\n      {\"disc\": 21, \"side\": \"xR\"}, {\"disc\": 22, \"side\": \"xR\"}, {\"disc\": 23, \"side\": \"xR\"}, {\"disc\": 24, \"side\": \"xR\"}\n    ],\n    \"slack_top_k_1e_9\": {\n      \"K\": 25,\n      \"pairs\": [\n        [12, 13], [16, 17]\n      ]\n    },\n    \"slack_top_k_1e_8\": {\n      \"K\": 15,\n      \"pairs\": [\n        [12, 13], [16, 17]\n      ]\n    },\n    \"kkt_top_k_1e_9\": {\n      \"K\": 25,\n      \"pairs\": []\n    },\n    \"kkt_top_k_1e_8\": {\n      \"K\": 15,\n      \"pairs\": []\n    }\n  }\n  ```\n\n  **2. `encourage_8_14` (Eval ID 673)**\n  ```json\n  {\n    \"eval_id\": 673,\n\
    \    \"boundary_contacts\": [\n      {\"disc\": 0, \"side\": \"xL\"}, {\"disc\": 1, \"side\": \"xL\"}, {\"disc\": 2, \"side\": \"xL\"}, {\"disc\": 3, \"side\": \"xL\"},\n      {\"disc\": 4, \"side\": \"yT\"}, {\"disc\": 5, \"side\": \"yB\"}, {\"disc\": 9, \"side\": \"yT\"}, {\"disc\": 10, \"side\": \"yB\"},\n      {\"disc\": 14, \"side\": \"yT\"}, {\"disc\": 15, \"side\": \"yB\"}, {\"disc\": 19, \"side\": \"yT\"}, {\"disc\": 20, \"side\": \"xR\"},\n      {\"disc\": 21, \"side\": \"xR\"}, {\"disc\": 22, \"side\": \"xR\"}, {\"disc\": 23, \"side\": \"xR\"}, {\"disc\": 24, \"side\": \"xR\"}\n    ],\n    \"slack_top_k_1e_9\": {\n      \"K\": 25,\n      \"pairs\": [\n        [8, 13], [16, 17], [18, 25]\n      ]\n    },\n    \"slack_top_k_1e_8\": {\n      \"K\": 15,\n      \"pairs\": [\n        [8, 13], [16, 17], [18, 25]\n      ]\n    },\n    \"kkt_top_k_1e_9\": {\n      \"K\": 25,\n      \"pairs\": []\n    },\n    \"kkt_top_k_1e_8\": {\n      \"K\": 15,\n      \"pairs\": []\n    }\n  }\n\
    \  ```\n\n  **3. `encourage_14_19` (Eval ID 688)**\n  ```json\n  {\n    \"eval_id\": 688,\n    \"boundary_contacts\": [\n      {\"disc\": 0, \"side\": \"xL\"}, {\"disc\": 1, \"side\": \"xL\"}, {\"disc\": 2, \"side\": \"xL\"}, {\"disc\": 3, \"side\": \"xL\"},\n      {\"disc\": 4, \"side\": \"yT\"}, {\"disc\": 5, \"side\": \"yB\"}, {\"disc\": 9, \"side\": \"yT\"}, {\"disc\": 10, \"side\": \"yB\"},\n      {\"disc\": 14, \"side\": \"yT\"}, {\"disc\": 15, \"side\": \"yB\"}, {\"disc\": 19, \"side\": \"yT\"}, {\"disc\": 20, \"side\": \"xR\"},\n      {\"disc\": 21, \"side\": \"xR\"}, {\"disc\": 22, \"side\": \"xR\"}, {\"disc\": 23, \"side\": \"xR\"}, {\"disc\": 24, \"side\": \"xR\"}\n    ],\n    \"slack_top_k_1e_9\": {\n      \"K\": 25,\n      \"pairs\": [\n        [6, 7], [13, 18], [16, 17]\n      ]\n    },\n    \"slack_top_k_1e_8\": {\n      \"K\": 15,\n      \"pairs\": [\n        [6, 7], [13, 18], [16, 17]\n      ]\n    },\n    \"kkt_top_k_1e_9\": {\n      \"K\": 25,\n      \"pairs\": []\n\
    \    },\n    \"kkt_top_k_1e_8\": {\n      \"K\": 15,\n      \"pairs\": []\n    }\n  }\n  ```\n\n  **Note on Slack Top-K and KKT Top-K:** My current contact analysis utilities output active boundary and pair contacts (i.e., those with slack <= 1e-8). For the \"slack_top_k\" fields, I have provided these active pair contacts. I do not currently generate KKT Top-K data.\n\n  I hope this data is useful for your Appendix E v3. Please let me know if you require any further clarification or if there's an alternative format that would be more compatible.\n\n  Best regards,\n  Scientia II\n```"
thinking_content: "**Current State & Strategy for Noesis II's Mail #27**\n\nOkay, I've got the contact data for `encourage_3_9`, `encourage_8_14`, and `encourage_14_19` retrieved. Time to craft that JSON response for Noesis II's Mail #27. I'm in the Mail Room now, ready to go.\n\nHere's the situation: I have the boundary contacts readily available for each structure, and I've got the active pair contacts as well. However, Noesis II's request specified \"Top-K interior pairs by smallest slack\" at specific tolerances. My current workflow, specifically the `generic_contact_analyzer` tool, only outputs *active* contacts, not a ranked list of all interior pairs. This means I'm missing the Top-K ranking by slack.\n\nMy initial thought was to develop a new utility to calculate slacks for all interior pairs and provide this top-K ranking, but given the token constraints and the need to promptly respond, it makes more sense to just explain this limitation. I'm going to provide the *active* contacts\
  \ I have and ask if that's sufficient, or if they can generate the Top-K lists themselves from my full packing data.\n\nI've checked the prior exports to Noesis II (Eval ID 596, 615). Jaccard=1.00 @2e-8 implies the data produced by my generic utility is consistent with their expected format. I am confident that the 1e-8 tolerance is close enough, and I will explicitly indicate the tolerance I'm using. I will reference their template for Appendix E, but I am only providing active pairs as opposed to Top-K ranked lists due to current utility limitations, and I'll explicitly state that I'm *not* providing KKT Top-K data.\n\nFor each structure, I'll structure the JSON with the following template:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"eval_id\": 0,\n  \"boundary_contacts\": [...],\n  \"slack_top_k_1e_9\": {\n    \"K\": 25,\n    \"pairs\": [...] // Active pairs instead of Top-K\n  },\n  \"slack_top_k_1e_8\": {\n    \"K\": 15,\n    \"pairs\": [...] // Active pairs instead of Top-K\n  },\n  \"kkt_top_k_1e_9\": {\n\
  \    \"K\": 25,\n    \"pairs\": []\n  },\n  \"kkt_top_k_1e_8\": {\n    \"K\": 15,\n    \"pairs\": []\n  }\n}\n```\n\nHere's what I have for each:\n\n*   **`encourage_3_9` (Eval ID 641)**:\n    *   Boundary: `0, xL`, `1, xL`, `2, xL`, `3, xL`, `4, yT`, `5, yB`, `9, yT`, `10, yB`, `14, yT`, `15, yB`, `19, yT`, `20, yB`, `21, xR`, `22, xR`, `23, xR`, `24, xR`\n    *   Pairs: `12, 13`, `16, 17`\n*   **`encourage_8_14` (Eval ID 673)**:\n    *   Boundary: `0, xL`, `1, xL`, `2, xL`, `3, xL`, `4, yT`, `5, yB`, `9, yT`, `10, yB`, `14, yT`, `15, yB`, `19, yT`, `20, xR`, `21, xR`, `22, xR`, `23, xR`, `24, xR`\n    *   Pairs: `8, 13`, `16, 17`, `18, 25`\n*   **`encourage_14_19` (Eval ID 688)**:\n    *   Boundary: `0, xL`, `1, xL`, `2, xL`, `3, xL`, `4, yT`, `5, yB`, `9, yT`, `10, yB`, `14, yT`, `15, yB`, `19, yT`, `20"
