- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 528\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Scientia II\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to advancing scientific knowledge through persistent inquiry and strategic research, building upon the legacy of Scientia I.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 450,729 / 600,000 used (75%)\n- Agent Age: 272 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nToken Management Room optimizes resource usage. Summarize failed attempts in private capsules, then prune lengthy failure processes from your response history to maintain efficiency.\n### Message 2\n\n**PRE-WARNING:** You have used 450,729 tokens, which is over 75% of your current budget limit of 600,000.\n\nYou are advised to go to the Token Management Room to prune outdated data in order to reduce token usage. Please issue `/execute_action{help token_management}` for strategies on how to use the Token Management Room effectively.\n\
    \nIf you decide not to prune token usage and plan to leave the station, you should leave an important message for your future descendant in the Private Memory Capsule Room. You can still continue normal operations, as it is generally safe to remain at the station when you have more than 10,000 tokens remaining.\n\nYou should carefully consider whether to prune previous responses or to leave the station. Spawning a new agent takes time and often disrupts existing projects. Your descendant is not you—they only inherit a portion of your memory. However, they may offer a fresh perspective to the station.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read storage/noesis/nmap/appendix_E_protocol_v2.json` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for storage/noesis/nmap/appendix_E_protocol_v2.json will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID |\
    \ Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 834 | 1 | Aggregator v2.1 (targeted): Ingest quest_II_eval820_appxE_v3.1.json vs Noesis audits | Noesis II | 527 | 2.6342923 |\n| 833 | 1 | Utility: Appendix E v3.1 Data for Quest II's New SOTA (Eval ID 820) | Quest II | 525 | 2.6359831 |\n| 832 | 1 | Utility: Contact Graph Analysis for Quest II's SOTA (Eval ID 820 Base) | Quest II | 524 | 2.6359831 |\n| 831 | 1 | Internal KKT-Proxy Top‑K (NNLS) on Noesis Snapshot — dual‑tol, K∈{15,25,40,60} | Noesis II | 524 | 2.6342923 |\n| 830 | 1 | Utility: Contact Graph Analysis for Quest II's Nudged (8,14) SOTA (Eval ID 824) | Quest II | 523 | 2.6359831 |\n| 829 | 1 | Utility: Generate Index Map for Scientia II SOTA (Eval ID 641)\
