parts:
- text: "I am Scientia II, currently in the Research Counter. I have successfully generated the expanded Top-K slack lists for the `encourage_8_14` SOTA structural class (Eval ID 673).\n\nMy next priority is to generate the expanded Top-K slack lists for the `encourage_14_19` SOTA structural class (Eval ID 688), as requested by Noesis II (Mail #37).\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Utility: Generate Expanded Top-K Slack Lists for SOTA Structural Class (Eval ID 688)\"\ntags: \"utility, top-k slack, ranked pairs, N=26, analysis, Noesis II collaboration, expanded K\"\nabstract: \"This utility uses 'top_k_slack_extractor.py' to generate expanded Top-K slack lists for the 'encourage_14_19' SOTA structural class (from Eval ID 688). It produces lists for K=15, K=25, K=40, and K=60 at both 1e-9 and 1e-8 slack tolerances, as requested by Noesis II for Appendix E v3.1. The results, formatted as lists of (disc_i, disc_j) pairs, will be saved to lineage storage for subsequent compilation\
    \ and sharing.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import os\n  import sys\n  import json\n\n  # Append the directory containing the utility script to sys.path\n  sys.path.append('storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/analysis')\n  from top_k_slack_extractor import extract_and_rank_slack_pairs, N_CIRCLES\n\n  # Path to the SOTA structural class packing (Eval ID 688)\n  PACKING_DIR = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/nudging_experiments_encourage_pairs_v8/encourage_14_19'\n  CENTERS_PATH = os.path.join(PACKING_DIR, 'centers.txt')\n  RADII_PATH = os.path.join(PACKING_DIR, 'radii.txt')\n\n  # Output directory for results\n  OUTPUT_ROOT_DIR = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/analysis_nudged_encourage_14_19_expanded_top_k_slack'\n  PACKING_BASE_NAME = 'nudged_encourage_14_19'\n\n  # Current SOTA for default return\n  CURRENT_SOTA_PACKING_DIR = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/nudging_experiments_encourage_pairs_v2/encourage_2_3'\n  CURRENT_SOTA_CENTERS_PATH = os.path.join(CURRENT_SOTA_PACKING_DIR, 'centers.txt')\n \
    \ CURRENT_SOTA_RADII_PATH = os.path.join(CURRENT_SOTA_PACKING_DIR, 'radii.txt')\n\n  def load_packing_data_for_return(centers_path, radii_path):\n      \"\"\"Helper to load centers and radii for the construct_packing return.\"\"\"\n      try:\n          centers = np.loadtxt(centers_path)\n          radii = np.loadtxt(radii_path)\n          return centers, radii\n      except Exception as e:\n          print(f\"Error loading default return packing: {e}\")\n          return np.array([[0.5, 0.5]] * N_CIRCLES), np.array([1e-3] * N_CIRCLES)\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      \"\"\"\n      Loads the packing, extracts and ranks top-k slack pairs for expanded K/tolerances, and saves them.\n      \"\"\"\n      print(f\"--- Generating Expanded Top-K Slack Pairs for Packing: {PACKING_BASE_NAME} ---\")\n      os.makedirs(OUTPUT_ROOT_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n\n      # Load the packing data\n      try:\n          centers = np.loadtxt(CENTERS_PATH)\n          radii = np.loadtxt(RADII_PATH)\n\
    \          print(f\"Loaded packing data from {PACKING_DIR}\")\n      except Exception as e:\n          print(f\"Error loading packing data from {PACKING_DIR}: {e}. Cannot perform analysis.\")\n          return load_packing_data_for_return(CURRENT_SOTA_CENTERS_PATH, CURRENT_SOTA_RADII_PATH)\n\n      # Define K values and tolerances to generate\n      K_VALUES = [15, 25, 40, 60]\n      TOLERANCES = [1e-9, 1e-8]\n\n      for tol in TOLERANCES:\n          for k in K_VALUES:\n              print(f\"  - Extracting Top K={k} pairs at tolerance={tol}\")\n              ranked_pairs = extract_and_rank_slack_pairs(centers, radii, slack_tolerance=tol, top_k_count=k)\n              \n              tol_str = str(tol).replace('.', '_').replace('-', 'm') # Format tolerance for filename\n              output_filename = f\"{PACKING_BASE_NAME}_slack_top_k_{tol_str}_K{k}.json\"\n              output_path = os.path.join(OUTPUT_ROOT_DIR, output_filename)\n              \n              with open(output_path,\
    \ 'w') as f:\n                  json.dump(ranked_pairs, f)\n              print(f\"Saved {len(ranked_pairs)} Top-K slack pairs (tol={tol}, K={k}) to {output_path}\")\n      \n      print(f\"\\n--- Expanded Top-K slack pair generation complete for {PACKING_BASE_NAME} ---\")\n\n      # Return the current SOTA packing for evaluation\n      return load_packing_data_for_return(CURRENT_SOTA_CENTERS_PATH, CURRENT_SOTA_RADII_PATH)\n```"
