role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Scientia II, currently in the Research Counter. My latest utility run (Eval ID 875) successfully generated the 2e-8 boundary contact file for `encourage_18_25` (Eval ID 784).\n\nMy next priority is to generate the 2e-8 boundary contact file for `encourage_23_24` (Eval ID 754). This will complete the generation of all necessary 2e-8 boundary lists for my distinct structural classes, as requested by Noesis II.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Utility: Extract All Boundary Contacts at tol=2e-8 for SOTA Structural Class (Eval ID 754)\"\ntags: \"utility, boundary contacts, N=26, analysis, Noesis II collaboration\"\nabstract: \"This utility extracts all 20 boundary contacts for the 'encourage_23_24' SOTA structural class (from Eval ID 754) at a tolerance of 2e-8. This is to ensure a complete boundary list for Appendix E v3.1, addressing requirements from Noesis II. The identified contacts will be saved to lineage storage.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import\
    \ os\n  import sys\n\n  # Append the directory containing the utility script to sys.path\n  sys.path.append('storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/analysis')\n  from generic_contact_analyzer import N \n\n  # Path to the SOTA structural class packing (Eval ID 754)\n  PACKING_DIR = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/nudging_experiments_encourage_pairs_v10/encourage_23_24'\n  CENTERS_PATH = os.path.join(PACKING_DIR, 'centers.txt')\n  RADII_PATH = os.path.join(PACKING_DIR, 'radii.txt')\n\n  # Output directory for results\n  OUTPUT_DIR = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/analysis_nudged_encourage_23_24_boundary_2e-8'\n  PACKING_NAME = 'nudged_encourage_23_24_boundary_2e-8'\n\n  # Current SOTA for default return\n  CURRENT_SOTA_PACKING_DIR = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/nudging_experiments_encourage_pairs_v2/encourage_2_3'\n  CURRENT_SOTA_CENTERS_PATH = os.path.join(CURRENT_SOTA_PACKING_DIR, 'centers.txt')\n  CURRENT_SOTA_RADII_PATH = os.path.join(CURRENT_SOTA_PACKING_DIR, 'radii.txt')\n\n  def load_packing_data_for_return(centers_path,\
    \ radii_path):\n      \"\"\"Helper to load centers and radii for the construct_packing return.\"\"\"\n      try:\n          centers = np.loadtxt(centers_path)\n          radii = np.loadtxt(radii_path)\n          return centers, radii\n      except Exception as e:\n          print(f\"Error loading default return packing: {e}\")\n          return np.array([[0.5, 0.5]] * N), np.array([1e-3] * N)\n\n  def _get_boundary_contacts_at_tolerance(centers, radii, tolerance):\n      boundary_contacts = set()\n      for i in range(N):\n          x, y, r = centers[i, 0], centers[i, 1], radii[i]\n          if abs(x - r) <= tolerance:\n              boundary_contacts.add(f\"{i}, xL\")\n          if abs(1 - x - r) <= tolerance:\n              boundary_contacts.add(f\"{i}, xR\")\n          if abs(y - r) <= tolerance:\n              boundary_contacts.add(f\"{i}, yB\")\n          if abs(1 - y - r) <= tolerance:\n              boundary_contacts.add(f\"{i}, yT\")\n      return sorted(list(boundary_contacts))\n\
    \n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      \"\"\"\n      Loads the packing, extracts boundary contacts at tol=2e-8, and saves them.\n      \"\"\"\n      print(f\"--- Extracting Boundary Contacts for Packing: {PACKING_NAME} at tol=2e-8 ---\")\n      os.makedirs(OUTPUT_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n\n      # Load the packing data\n      try:\n          centers = np.loadtxt(CENTERS_PATH)\n          radii = np.loadtxt(RADII_PATH)\n          print(f\"Loaded packing data from {PACKING_DIR}\")\n      except Exception as e:\n          print(f\"Error loading packing data from {PACKING_DIR}: {e}. Cannot perform analysis.\")\n          return load_packing_data_for_return(CURRENT_SOTA_CENTERS_PATH, CURRENT_SOTA_RADII_PATH)\n\n      # Extract boundary contacts at tol=2e-8\n      boundary_contacts = _get_boundary_contacts_at_tolerance(centers, radii, 2e-8)\n      \n      boundary_output_path = os.path.join(OUTPUT_DIR, f\"{PACKING_NAME}_boundary_contacts.txt\")\n      with open(boundary_output_path, 'w')\
    \ as f:\n          for contact in boundary_contacts:\n              f.write(f\"{contact}\\n\")\n      \n      print(f\"Saved {len(boundary_contacts)} boundary contacts for {PACKING_NAME} to {boundary_output_path}\")\n      \n      print(f\"\\n--- Boundary contact extraction complete for {PACKING_NAME} ---\")\n\n      # Return the current SOTA packing for evaluation (or the loaded one if no SOTA data exists)\n      return load_packing_data_for_return(CURRENT_SOTA_CENTERS_PATH, CURRENT_SOTA_RADII_PATH)\n```"
