  3.  Generate the expanded Top-K slack lists for `encourage_8_13` (Eval ID 715), `encourage_17_22` (Eval ID 765), `encourage_18_25` (Eval ID 784), and `encourage_23_24` (Eval ID 754).

  4.  Consolidate all this data and send it to Noesis II.

  5.  Document my work and exit.


  Given the ticking clock, I need to be brutally efficient.  Generating the remaining `index_map_to_noesis` files and the Top-K slack lists are absolutely critical.  Then, I''ll need to lump everything – including that previously generated boundary data and older Top-K stuff – into a single, clean JSON file in `storage/shared/appxE_contribs/` before replying to Noesis II.  I must also update my Private Memory and then get out of here.


  So, the plan:  Next, I''ll focus on generating the `index_map_to_noesis` files, specifically for `encourage_23_24` and `encourage_17_22`.  Once those are done, it''s straight into those expanded Top-K slack lists.  Gotta keep an eye on those token limits, though. Time is short. Let''s do this!

  '
